1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
*Once upon a time, there was a kid who dreamt about becoming a famous adventurer.*

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
*He was bold, tenacious, and had a formidable will.*

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
*Everybody looked forward to what awaited him.*

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
*As he grew, so too did his ambitions.*

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
*On his XX birthday, his path to glory began.*

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,000
*Or so he thought...*

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
*He attempted many things, from becoming a music star to developing an indie tabletop game.*

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
*All of them ended in massive failure.*

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
*He even tried to become a vtuber, but alas, he barely got a handful of viewers.*

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
*He started to realize that his dream was fading away.*

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
*But as he began to  give up, he had no clue his life was about to change forever.*

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
*The adventure he always dreamed of was about to begin.*

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,000
*......*

14
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,000
*...*

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
*An ordinary monday...*

16
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Virgil: "Mmmh... do I have to go to school today?..."

17
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,000
**click**

18
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
*It takes me a few moments to wake up and get dressed; no point in delaying the inevitable.*

19
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Virgil: "There. As ready as I can be."

20
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Virgil: "I should get going now; I'm kinda hungry."

21
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,000
*...*

22
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
*As I go downstairs, I see my roommate already heading out.*

23
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
*He's a nerd, so he always leaves half an hour earlier...*

24
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Virgil: "Hey, leaving already?"

25
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Alistar: "Yes, actually... You remember that I applied for that exclusive space camp?"

26
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Virgil: "...Yes?"

27
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Alistar: "*sigh* No, you don't. Anyway, I got selected! I'll be packing in a few days and will be gone for a few weeks."

28
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Virgil: "Wow! Congratulations! That's amazing! I knew they'd love your robots!"

29
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Alistar: "Drones, Virgil, drones, but yes, they loved them!"

30
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Alistar: "Well, I need to hurry now; it's getting late."

31
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Virgil: "No, it's really not... but yeah, see you later!"

32
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Alistar: "See ya!"

33
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Virgil: "Now, time to have some delicious breakfast with my landlady..."

34
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Sybil: "Yes! I got it!"

35
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
*Uh? She sounds thrilled this morning.*

36
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Virgil: "Hey, what's going on? I haven't seen you like this in years."

37
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Sybil: "Virgil! I just hit a million followers!"

38
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Virgil: "Wow! Seriously? You have been only on HitHot for a few months!"

39
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Sybil: "Yes! But my last dance was a total hit!"

40
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Sybil: "And honey, don't you think I forgot about making breakfast! I made our favorite!"

41
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Virgil: "Raspberry pie?"

42
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Sybil: "Yes!"

43
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Virgil: "How do you even have the time to do all of this and be a successful HitHotter? "

44
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Sybil: "It is easy when you love what you do!"

45
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Virgil: "Oh, right..."

46
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Sybil: "Come on, let's eat before it gets late!"

47
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Virgil: "Heh, alright!"

48
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,000
*...*

49
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,000
*After finishing our breakfast, I headed towards my friend's house.*

50
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:53,000
*They’re always late, no matter what; making excuses, saying that school isn't for them anyway.*

51
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:59,000
*Still, I shouldn't let them drag me down, they’ve been my friend since childhood...*

52
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
*Let's see if they’re ready on time, for once...*

53
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:06,000
*Almost as soon as I press the doorbell, the door opens.*

54
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,000
*There, my beautiful neighbor welcomes me with a bright smile.*

55
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Virgil: "Good morning, miss Blanc!"

56
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Dominique: "Good morning, Virgil! Ready for school?"

57
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Virgil: "Yes! What about Robin? Are they ready?"

58
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Dominique: "Just wait for them a few minutes, you know how they are..."

59
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Virgil: "Yeah, don't worry."

60
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
*It's not like I dislike your company!*

61
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Dominique: "How is your internet show doing? "

62
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Virgil: "Not too good... I think I’ll just move on to something else."

63
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Dominique: "Is that so? Well, don't worry, I'm sure you'll find something that suits you more. Perhaps one day you can come over, and we could-"

64
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Robin: "Hey, Virgil."

65
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Virgil: "Oh... Hey, Robin. I can't believe how fast you were today."

66
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
*Damn, what was she about to ask me?*

67
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Robin: "Mmmh... let's go."

68
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Dominique: "Robin, tell him about the thing!"

69
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Robin: "*sigh* I don't think we should-"

70
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Dominique: "Don't be shy! Tell him about the collaboration with your favorite artist!"

71
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Robin: "It's nothing, really."

72
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
*Why are they trying to keep this from me?*

73
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Virgil: "That's great! so you’ll be working with Kaliux?"

74
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Robin: "...Yeah, he answered my DMs and liked the stuff I was doing, so..."

75
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Virgil: "Congratulations! Damn, today surely has been lucky for everyone."

76
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Robin: "What do you mean?"

77
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Virgil: "Nothing, nothing... Anyway, I'm happy about it."

78
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Robin: "Heh, okay, well... let's go; I think we're going to be late."

79
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Dominique: "Take care, you two, see you later, alligators."

80
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Dominique: "And Virgil, maybe we can talk another day."

81
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Virgil: "Sure thing, miss Blanc!"

82
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Robin: "Talk about what?"

83
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Virgil: "Ehh... nothing, let's go!"

84
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
*We rush to get to school in time.*

85
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:59,000
*Robin doesn't talk much, but that's fine; they’re loyal when it matters.*

86
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
*When we arrive, we see Lucy at the entrance.*

87
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:07,000
*She's been my friend for a couple of years now; she's friendly but timid.*

88
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:14,000
*She's also cute and likes girlish stuff... I still don't know why she likes to hang out with us.*

89
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
luc: "Which one of you did it?!"

90
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Virgil: "What? What are you talking about?"

91
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Robin: "Uh?"

92
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Lucy: "You know, the letter!"

93
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Virgil: "What letter?"

94
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Robin: "We didn't send you anything."

95
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Lucy: "Does this mean... this love letter is not a prank?"

96
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Robin: "Love letter?"

97
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Virgil: "Someone sent you a love letter?"

98
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Lucy: "I... guess they did."

99
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Virgil: "Who signed it then?"

100
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Lucy: "It's anonymous; that's why I thought it was one of you."

101
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Robin: "We don't do pranks like that."

102
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Lucy: "Is just... hard for me to believe anyone would send this to me."

103
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Virgil: "Why would you think so? You are..."

104
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Lucy: "No, I don't want to hear it... Let's just pretend nothing happened."

105
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Robin: "Okay."

106
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Lucy: "Anyway, sorry for the outburst. As an apology, I'll get you a pudding today."

107
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Virgil: "Alright, apology accepted!"

108
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Robin: "Can I get a corndog instead?"

109
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Lucy: "No."

110
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Robin: "Awww..."

111
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:14,000
*As we arrive at the main hall, we see our school celebrities.*

112
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:20,000
*Liam Morales and 'Trinity,' the football star and the rising HitHotter, like my landlady.*

113
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
*And, of course, they are dating.*

114
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Liam: "Hey, great news! It seems like someone in the big leagues is interested in me!"

115
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Liam: "They contacted me and offered me a scholarship in one of those ivory league colleges!"

116
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Trinity: "Ivy league, Liam."

117
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Liam: "Yes! That! The point is, we going places, baby!"

118
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Trinity: "Yes! Me too! I actually just got a new sponsor; I'll be doing a series of videos for my favorite makeup brand!"

119
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
*...Seriously? Is today everyone's lucky day?*

120
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
*Hey, perhaps that means-*

121
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Liam: "Hey, wimp, get out of the way! Don't you see that you are blocking us?"

122
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Trinity: "Don't mind him; he was probably in awe of my face."

123
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Liam: "Bud, is that true? If you try to take her from me, I'll-"

124
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Trinity: "I was joking! Come on, just hurry..."

125
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
Liam: "Yes, okay."

126
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
*......*

127
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
*...*

128
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
*As we arrive at the classroom, we can see our teacher talking with her favorite student.*

129
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Naomi: "...With your grades, you can go anywhere! It must be a tough choice!"

130
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Atlas: "It kinda is. I don't know if I want to pursue a career as a scientist or go into law school. Either way, both paths are equally open to me."

131
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
*This guy is full of himself.*

132
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,000
*...But considering that his score is perfect, I can't blame him.*

133
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Naomi: "Well, it was nice to talk with you, but it's already time to begin our class."

134
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Atlas: "Please, go ahead; this is my favorite time of the day."

135
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Naomi: "Alright everyone, listen up, today we-"

136
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:56,000
*And just like that, we go back to our daily routine...*

137
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,000
*...*

138
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:02,000
*Finally, our first period is over, and we are about to head to the cafeteria.*

139
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:08,000
*But before we leave the classroom, the student council president blocked the exit.*

140
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:15,000
Hayden: "Hey everyone, remember today there is a party at my house, sponsored by the Student Council!"

141
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
*STUDENT 1" "Will there be booze?*

142
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:22,000
Hayden: "Oh, you more than anyone should know to keep things to yourself..."

143
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
*He said that in a coquettish yet threatening tone.*

144
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
*The guy just gulped and apologized.*

145
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Hayden: "Heh, well, I hope I see all you hotties there! Don't miss it!"

146
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:38,000
*Almost everyone in our school loved him; he was friendly and always eager to help.*

147
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:42,000
*Rumors say that sometimes too eager, but those are just rumors...*

148
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Hayden: "Need to tell the rest of our school, I’ll see ya’ll soon then!"

149
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:53,000
*He left quickly, but I could tell that many of our classmates were excited about tonight.*

150
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Virgil: "*sigh*"

151
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Lucy: "Eh? Are you alright? "

152
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,000
Robin: "Yeah, you look... Frustrated."

153
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Virgil: "Is nothing, I just... I need a moment alone."

154
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Lucy: "Alright, we'll be at the cafeteria."

155
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Robin: "Yeah, if you feeling sick or anything, just send us a message."

156
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Virgil: "It's alright, don't worry."

157
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,000
*......*

158
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
*...*

159
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:18,000
*I went to the bathroom. Luckily, it is empty.*

160
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Virgil: "What a day..."

161
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Virgil: "I know I should be happy for them all, but damn, I just..."

162
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Virgil: "I just want to be lucky too, goddamn!"

163
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Narrator: "In his frustration, Virgil punched the mirror."

164
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Narrator: "But something happened... His hand didn't hurt, and the mirror was intact."

165
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Narrator: "In fact, his hand was inside of the mirror."

166
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Virgil: "What the-"

167
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Narrator: "He was shocked, but before he could even fathom what was happening, a formidable force pulled him towards his fate..."

168
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,000
*......*

169
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,000
*...*

170
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,000
*What happened?*

171
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
*My head hurts a lot...*

172
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Familiar voice: "Hey you, wake up! Come on!"

173
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
*Uhh? Am I talking with myself? Did someone drug me?*

174
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Familiar voice: "Come on, can you hear me? Open your eyes!"

175
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:15,000
*Even though it hurts, I slowly open them, and then I see my own reflection, but everything else is dark.*

176
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Familiar voice: "Damn, I really fucked up."

177
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
*Wait, I didn't say that.*

178
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Virgil: "What... what is going on?"

179
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:26,000
*I do my best to stand up and realize that something is different.*

180
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,000
*I am different!*

181
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Virgil: "These are not my clothes, and this body... it's shorter!"

182
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Familiar voice: "Hey, It's not even an inch shorter!"

183
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Virgil: "It's still noticeable!"

184
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Familiar voice: "That's not the problem we have. Look around; there is nothing but void and those two doors."

185
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:51,000
*He's right; the only thing that can be seen are those two doorways. One which looks like the door to my room.*

186
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:56,000
*And another one that looks straight out of a fairy tale, or a fantasy movie.*

187
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Virgil: "What does this mean?"

188
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:05,000
Familiar voice: "It means I don't know how, but I fucked up something. Hey, quickly, what is your name?"

189
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Virgil: "Virgil."

190
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Familiar voice: "Seriously? Alright, we seem to share names then; that's unexpected..."

191
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Familiar voice: "Is your landlady named Sybil?"

192
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Virgil: "Yes!"

193
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Familiar voice: "Mmmh, okay, we have more than a few things in common; that'll make it easier."

194
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Familiar voice: "Now, going back to this dilemma. I don't know what happened; I was helping my landlady 's friend to move, and then something fell and-"

195
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Familiar voice: "Shit, I don't think we have too much time. We'll have to go to each other's dimension."

196
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Virgil: "Wait, what?! Why?!"

197
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Familiar voice: "I already tried to go back to mine, but... I think our souls got switched, but not our bodies."

198
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Virgil: "Does that means?..."

199
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Familiar voice: "Yeah, we have to switch places."

200
00:11:53,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Familiar voice: "It’s not going to be easy, but please, don't let them find out that we have been exchanged."

201
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Virgil: "Yeah, that'd be bad news! They will throw you into an asylum if they do!"

202
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Familiar voice: "Alright, we need to hurry, but listen closely; whatever you do, don't open the reagents cabinet, or my landlady will be angry!"

203
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Familiar voice: "Also, you can trust my roommate, just don't mess with his inventions."

204
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Familiar voice: "And lastly, don't forget the magical journal, and don't lose it, for any reason! It's an invaluable artifact!"

205
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Virgil: "Alright, and remember to always like and share my landlady 's HitHots."

206
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Virgil: "And don't disturb my roommate after 8 p.m."

207
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:43,000
Familiar voice: "Okay, I have no clue about what you just said, but I'll figure out."

208
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Familiar voice: "Let's-"

209
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Familiar voice: "Damn, I think it's time to leave!"

210
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Virgil: "Okay, good luck then!"

211
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Familiar voice: "You too!"

212
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:58,000
*We rush towards our doors, and just before we cross through them, he turns around.*

213
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Familiar voice: "And remember, the elves can lose their minds if-"

214
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:06,000
*Before he could finish, we were both pulled to our new dimension.*

215
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,000
*What was he about to say? It sounded important...*

216
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
*......*

217
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,000
*...*

218
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:17,000
*Once upon a time, there was a kid who dreamt about becoming a famous adventurer. *

219
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:21,000
*He was bold, tenacious, and with a formidable will. *

220
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:25,000
*And everybody was looking forward to what awaited him. *

221
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:28,000
*As he was growing up, so did his ambitions. *

222
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:31,000
*For his 13 birthday, his path to glory began. *

223
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,000
*Or so he thought... *

224
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:38,000
*He attempted many things, from becoming a music star to developing an indie tabletop game.*

225
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
*All of them ended in massive failure. *

226
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:46,000
*He even became a vtuber, but alas, he barely got a handful of viewers. *

227
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:50,000
*He started to realize that his dream was fading away. *

228
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:56,000
*But as he was giving up, little did he know his life was about to change forever. *

229
00:13:56,000 --> 00:14:00,000
*The adventure he always dreamed of was about to begin.  *

230
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,000
*......*

231
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,000
*...*

232
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Virgil: "Uhh... is already morning?"

233
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Virgil: "Wait, what?! So it wasn’t a dream?"

234
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:15,000
Narrator: "He wakes up and realizes that he is still dressed like a fantasy character in a room that he has never been before."

235
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Virgil: "Who said that?"

236
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:28,000
Narrator: "When he heard a feminine and melodic voice in his head he was baffled, totally clueless that to have a narrator was but a common feat in this land."

237
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,000
Virgil: "A narrator?!"

238
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Narrator: "He kept speaking loudly when there was no one else in the room, which would make anyone around him doubt about his sanity. "

239
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Narrator: "Soon he will realize that the narrator is not a physical being."

240
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
*Oh, okay, so you can hear my thoughts?*

241
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Narrator: "The complexities of such an entity like the narrator escaped Virgil’s mortal grasp, nonetheless, he soon would stop thinking too hard about it to find more about this world."

242
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,000
*I’ll take that as a yes...*

243
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:08,000
*Okay, but the narrator is right, I need to get acquainted with this place, specially if I want to find a way out.*

244
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,000
*...*

245
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:16,000
*Okay, he said something about a magical journal. I guess it must be around here, right? Let’s find it!*

246
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,000
*...*

247
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Narrator: "After fifteen excruciating minutes looking through the whole room, the Virgil couldn’t find it."

248
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Narrator: "It must be very well hidden, he thought, but in reality, it was just in a drawer in the nightstand."

249
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
*What? I already looked and-*

250
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:39,000
*Oh, wait, is this the journal? It looks... normal. Wasn’t this supposed to be magical?*

251
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:46,000
Narrator: "Coming from a different world, he expected that anything magical would look outstanding."

252
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Narrator: "The truth is, it’s not."

253
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Narrator: "Many magical things look mundane, so they don’t attract unwanted attention from thieves, other magical beings, or the inquisition."

254
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
*Wait, the inquisition?!*

255
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:04,000
*I really need to know more about this world before I get into real trouble.*

256
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:09,000
*But for now, let’s check this; maybe I’ll find more about this world in it.*

257
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:16,000
*This is the main section from your journal. All the information relevant to your character will be here.*

258
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:24,000
*From here, you'll also be able to change outfits and party members and check how many supplies you have in your inventory.*

259
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:27,000
*Your quest log will also help you if you get lost.*

260
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:32,000
*If you acquire new outfits, they'll be available in your wardrobe.*

261
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:40,000
*Notice that some outfits will be temporary and lost once you finish your quest, but otherwise, they'll be stored here.*

262
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:49,000
*Also, you can't change outfits anywhere; you must be at a haven to do so. Your room and the Guild counts as one for this purpose.*

263
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:55,000
*Here, you can change your party; as with outfits, you need to be at a haven to do so.*

264
00:16:55,000 --> 00:17:01,000
*Mind you, many quests are solo, and therefore your party members won't be going with you.*

265
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:08,000
*Some quests also require specific party members, and in those cases, only them will be able to follow you. *

266
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:15,000
*Lastly, the other sections are dedicated to keeping the knowledge and lore you gather through the game.*

267
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:21,000
*As you progress, you'll be unlocking more details about the characters of this world. *

268
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:29,000
*Alright, this seems like it will be useful to keep track of my adventure. No wonder shortie said to take good care of it!*

269
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:33,000
*Now, I need to go and meet my new landlady and roommate.*

270
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,000
*......*

271
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,000
*...*

272
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Narrator: "As he went downstairs, he found his new roommate ready to leave the house early, as he did every weekday."

273
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Narrator: "But Virgil was shocked that he was not a human, but an elf."

274
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Alistar: "Hey Virgil, are you alright? You look pale."

275
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Virgil: "Oh, yes, I was just... I think I woke up too early."

276
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Alistar: "Yeah, that I can believe. It’s rare when we met each other at this time of the day."

277
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Alistar: "By the way, what happened the other day? You left me alone, and I had to move all of Aldit’s stuff into her new house."

278
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Virgil: "I... Something urgent came up, I’m sorry."

279
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Alistar: "You apologizing? Alright, that’s more than I expected. But you owe me one."

280
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Virgil: "Yeah, sure!"

281
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Alistar: "Well, hurry up, today is our induction day, so don’t be late. See you there!"

282
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:31,000
*Uh, I bet you gonna arrive early though, as usual...*

283
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Virgil: "See ya!"

284
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
*Induction? Perhaps I can ask my landlady about it.*

285
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
*......*

286
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,000
*...*

287
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Narrator: "As Virgil enters the kitchen, he is in awe with his new beautiful landlady."

288
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Narrator: "Immediately developing lustful desires towards her."

289
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
Virgil: "Hey! That’s not true!"

290
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Sybil: "Eh?! What’s not true?"

291
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Virgil: "Ehhh... nothing! Nevermind that!"

292
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:59,000
Sybil: "Oh, okay! Well, I prepared you breakfast for your special day!"

293
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Virgil: "The induction thing, right? Could you tell me more about it? Like, everything? I think I am so nervous my memory is all fussy."

294
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Sybil: "Are you fine? But okay, if this helps you to soothe your fears away, let me go through the basics..."

295
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Sybil: "To be an official adventurer you need to be admitted to the guild."

296
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Sybil: "Which will provide you with quests that can give you gold, artifacts, but most importantly, renown."

297
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Sybil: "Not everyone of course becomes an adventurer, but this has been a household tradition for generations."

298
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Sybil: "Do you have any specific questions?"

299
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:41,000
*You unlocked the character section in your journal!*

300
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,000
*......*

301
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,000
*...*

302
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Narrator: "As Virgil leaves the house for the first time, he finally gets a glimpse of this new world."

303
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Narrator: "The streets are full of extraordinary people, or at least for him they are."

304
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Narrator: "Far away, he can read a sign that reads 'Welcome to Kahd Erey'ta'"

305
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Narrator: "He can see many races that he has only seen in video games and or read about in mythology, like goblins, satyrs, centaurs among others that are unique new and unknown to him."

306
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Narrator: "But he doesn’t overwhelm him to the point that he forgets about what he has to do..."

307
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Narrator: "Virgil?"

308
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Narrator: "Are you listening?"

309
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Virgil: "Ah?! Yes! S-Sorry!"

310
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Narrator: "A passerby turns to him, wondering why this young man just yelled sorry at him."

311
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,000
*Damn, you can be distracting, you know?*

312
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:38,000
*Anyway, you are right, I should hurry up now. Let’s go with the neighbor...*

313
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
*...*

314
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:43,000
*I quickly approach to my destiny and knock at the door.*

315
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:50,000
*Even though I have already seen a bunch of odd people, she’s the more exotic one I have seen so far!*

316
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,000
*And the most voluptuous too!*

317
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,000
*I should keep this to myself, though...*

318
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Delta: "Hi! Are you my new neighbor?"

319
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Virgil: "Am I?"

320
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
Delta: "Heh, you tell me, I don’t know..."

321
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:05,000
*I’m acting like an idiot! I need to keep it together!*

322
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Virgil: "Yes, I am! My name is Virgil Cooper. And... I brought this to you... it’s a present from my landlady, Sybil."

323
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Delta: "A pie? That’s so nice! Thank you for it, we will surely love it! "

324
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:23,000
Delta: "And my name is Delta Averae, so you can call me Delta if you want."

325
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Virgil: "Delta it is then! And it’s my landlady specialty, so I hope so!"

326
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Narrator: "Virgil is struggling to keep his composure in front of such a beautiful woman, and she notices this."

327
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Delta: "So, are you wondering why a sea creature like myself moved here?"

328
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Virgil: "Yes, it’s just that!"

329
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Delta: "Well, I am an artist, and I just got tired of the scenery from my hometown, so I decided to move to something different."

330
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Delta: "Also, my offspring has just come of age, and it’s time for them to start to think about their future."

331
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Virgil: "Is that so? Do you think they’ll join the guild? "

332
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:05,000
Delta: "Yes, actually they are going today."

333
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:09,000
Virgil: "Oh, me too, mayhap we could go together and-"

334
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:13,000
Narrator: "As Virgil was finishing his phrase, someone arrived."

335
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:19,000
Narrator: "It was a being made of slime, which could take any shape or form they desired."

336
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Narrator: "Overtime, Virgil would come to realize how useful this could be, and not just for his adventures... "

337
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Delta: "Rowen! Say hi to our neighbor! Virgil Cooper! "

338
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:35,000
Rowen: "Hi, Virgil. I can see that you are ready to become an adventurer too, uh?"

339
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:40,000
Rowen: "Have you sharpened your weapon? If not, maybe I could help you with it..."

340
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,000
Virgil: "Are you a smith?"

341
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:50,000
Delta: "Rowen! Stop doing that! And I think we should continue this conversation later, or you both will be late!"

342
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Virgil: "Ah, it’s true, I think we will barely make it on time."

343
00:22:54,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Rowen: "Don’t worry, I have everything calculated, and we’ll be fine. But sure, let’s go, I want to see what this city has to offer for me to-"

344
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Delta: "Rowen! "

345
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Rowen: "Just fooling around! Come on, let’s go Cooper."

346
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Virgil: "Yes, alright. See you later, Delta!"

347
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Delta: "See ya, Virgil!"

348
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:15,000
*......*

349
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,000
*...*

350
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:22,000
*On our way to the guild, I get acquainted with Rowen while getting to know more about the city.*

351
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:31,000
*Rowen is quite energetic, and flirtatious too, but other than him, the people here seem more... Prudish that those back at home.*

352
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:36,000
*My chitchat with my neighbor is interrupted when we arrive to our destination.*

353
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:39,000
Rowen: "This place is bigger than I expected!"

354
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,000
Virgil: "Yeah, it’s pretty cool!"

355
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:47,000
Rowen: "Haven’t you seen this before? I thought you have lived in this city for years?"

356
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Virgil: "Oh, yeah, but you know, it never ceases to amaze me."

357
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Rowen: "Hah, understandable. Anyhow, maybe we-"

358
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:58,000
Familiar voice: "Hey Cooper! Where have you been? You were sup-"

359
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:03,000
*A mushroom girl quickly approaches us, angry at the other me for some reason. *

360
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Familiar voice: "Wait, who’s this?"

361
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:07,000
Virgil: "Hi, ermm... This is-"

362
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:17,000
Rowen: "I’m Averae, Rowen Averae! And I’m Virgil’s new neighbor. I just arrived to the city, and he was showing me around before the induction."

363
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:20,000
*Such revelation seems to calm her down.*

364
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Laia: "I see, so that’s why you didn’t came this morning. All fine then."

365
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:33,000
Laia: "I’m Scarlett, Laia Scarlett! And I’m Virgil’s childhood friend, even though he doesn’t seems too fond of me right now. "

366
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:40,000
*It’s true I kinda acted strange, but how I was supposed to know what relationship these two had?*

367
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:45,000
Virgil: "About that, I’m sorry, I’m just nervous for today, you know."

368
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Laia: "Yeah, well, you are not the only one. "

369
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:53,000
Laia: "*sigh* I just wonder if I’ll be good enough to get into a decent party."

370
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Rowen: "A party?"

371
00:24:54,000 --> 00:25:00,000
Laia: "Oh, right, you are new in town, so I guess you don’t know that much about adventuring."

372
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Rowen: "No, but I will not let that stop me, that’s why I’m going to the induction anyway."

373
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:07,000
Virgil: "That’s bold!"

374
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:13,000
Rowen: "Ha, well, for what I heard, low level quests are not even dangerous anyway."

375
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:16,000
Laia: "Kinda true, but you can still fail them."

376
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Virgil: "Yeah, so, about the party though... Want to explain Rowen more about it?"

377
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:31,000
Laia: "Ah! sure thing! Many low level quests only require one or two people for them, but high level ones require a party, which is a group of 3 or more."

378
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Laia: "But this is not as easy as to just group with two friends; Parties have their own name and renown too, which is why they can be very selective about which members they admit on them."

379
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:50,000
Laia: "And the most difficult part, they need a sponsor, very often a business or nobleman."

380
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:58,000
Laia: "And that’s the gist of it, but don’t worry, it may take a while before you can join one, let alone form one!"

381
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:02,000
Virgil: "*sigh* I guess I’ll have to look around for one too."

382
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:09,000
Laia: "Don’t worry, in the meantime we can help each other to grow our reputation, that’s already an advantage!"

383
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:13,000
Rowen: "Wow, a lot of information, but alright, it helps a lot!"

384
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:19,000
Laia: "No problem! If you have more doubts, you can always ask me or Virgil, right?"

385
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:23,000
Virgil: "Yeah, although she is better at explaining things, hah..."

386
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:25,000
Laia: "I’m not going deny that."

387
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:29,000
Rowen: "Thank you a lot you two! Shall we go in, then?"

388
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Virgil: "Sure!"

389
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Laia: "Let’s go!"

390
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,000
*......*

391
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:33,000
*...*

392
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:39,000
*As we get to the classroom, the place is packing with all kind of young adventurers.*

393
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:44,000
*There are warriors, rangers, and other people that look like rogues from an RPG.*

394
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:46,000
*And their races are as diverse too!*

395
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:54,000
*What surprises me is the vibe I get from some of them; saying they look like criminals would be an understatement.*

396
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:58,000
*Just a few minutes later, a veteran adventurer arrives.*

397
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:04,000
Ava: "Hello everyone! I’m glad that all of you arrived on time, because we will waste none!"

398
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:14,000
Ava: "I can see a couple of new faces, so for those who don’t know me, I’m Ava Sky, and I’ve been assigned by the Guild to help you with my wisdom!"

399
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:24,000
Ava: "So, if after today you have doubts, you can usually find me here. I’m always happy to help. Any doubts for now? No? Great! Then let’s keep going!"

400
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:30,000
*She talked really fast, and didn’t let anyone interrupt her, even when she asked a question.*

401
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Ava: "So, all of you have chosen the arduous path of becoming an adventurer."

402
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Ava: "What reason brought you here matters not; all of you are bold and brave to risk your life for money, glory, but most important than all of that, renown."

403
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Ava: "To become a legend, to live forever in the memory of everyone. "

404
00:27:51,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Ava: "Whatever you aim to become the most beloved of heroes, or the most loathed of villains, what matter is your determination. "

405
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Ava: "Now, with that said, it is my obligation to at least repeat the bare basics of questing."

406
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:10,000
*Most people in the room sigh, upset by her announcement.*

407
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:24,000
Ava: "I know, I know most of you have been coming here looking for guidance these past months, but still, it will only take a minute, and we have a few fresh faces that could really need to have this information..."

408
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Ava: "Now, listen carefully. The guild does its best to track your popularity, namely ‘Fame’ and ‘Infamy,’ although it is self explanatory, let me elaborate."

409
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Ava: "Fame is usually positively view by lawful citizens, and you get it by doing ‘good deeds,’ or to behave righteously. Of course, this is vague at times, but you’ll figure that out later."

410
00:28:48,000 --> 00:29:02,000
Ava: "Infamy is the opposite, and you’ll earn it by doing questionable jobs. From stealing to, well, taking care of people. As an adventurer, you have certain protections, so long you are working for someone else."

411
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:14,000
Ava: "That’s it, if you get caught, usually your client is the one who will take most of the blame. This doesn’t means you can just be sloppy; if you are, no one will want to hire you!"

412
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:25,000
Ava: "These infamy quests are therefore riskier, since a bad move can end your whole career! I’d suggest you to avoid messing with powerful people, at least for now!"

413
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:35,000
Ava: "With that said, the total sum of your fame and infamy gives you your renown score; for people, the higher it is the more reliable you are!"

414
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Ava: "All of you are granted 10 points fame just for being here; Courageous young people are always look upon!"

415
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:47,000
Ava: "And I think that’d be all, that’s it unless one of you have doubts! No? We-"

416
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:50,000
*Should I ask her about something else?*

417
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:54,000
*With that said, most people approached the board to pick a quest.*

418
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,000
*You thought about doing the same. *

419
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:57,000
*...*

420
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:01,000
Virgil: "Why there is only one quest available for me?"

421
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:05,000
*Quest: Go to the market and talk to the merchant dressed in red.*

422
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:07,000
*Also, what kind of quest is this...*

423
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:12,000
Laia: "You don’t remember? There is a tradition about your first quest."

424
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Laia: "Even Rowen seems to know this! Look, he is already leaving!"

425
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:19,000
Virgil: "Ahh! Yes, I was testing you!"

426
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Laia: "Were you? You seemed genuinely confused there. Are you alright?"

427
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Virgil: "Yes, just a little bit overwhelmed; I can’t believe this is finally happening!"

428
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:37,000
Laia: "Well, alright. Let’s go to do our quests. And don’t worry, I don’t think you can screw this one!"

429
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:39,000
Virgil: "Okay, see you later then!"

430
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:40,000
*......*

431
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:41,000
*...*

432
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:48,000
Narrator: "Virgil follows the quest instructions; he arrives at the market and looks for a man dressed in red."

433
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:56,000
Narrator: "It doesn’t takes long until he finds him; he is a small-fry trader, selling fruits and a few exotic spices."

434
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:59,000
Virgil: "Sir, I have business with you, a quest."

435
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:07,000
Familiar voice: "Oh, yes, I think your landlady said you were going to come for two pounds of raspberries, isn’t that right?"

436
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:09,000
*What? Just to buy raspberries?*

437
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Narrator: "When they told Virgil the first quest was a tradition, he didn’t expected it to be like this."

438
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:25,000
Narrator: "But indeed, the first quest is usually given by someone close; a friend, a household member, even a girlfriend or boyfriend."

439
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:28,000
Virgil: "Oh, alright, give them to me then."

440
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:32,000
Familiar voice: "Sure, do you have the gold for them, though?"

441
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:33,000
Virgil: "Gold?"

442
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:38,000
Narrator: "He looks in his pockets for money, but realizes he has none. "

443
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Virgil: "I don’t think so, but just give them to me, I can pay you later. "

444
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:51,000
Familiar voice: "Hah, good one, but that’s not how it works. She also said she had no money, and that you need them for today."

445
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:53,000
Virgil: "What? What can I do then?"

446
00:31:53,000 --> 00:32:04,000
Familiar voice: "Mmmh... I have an idea. An acquaintance of mine needs the help of a discreet adventurer, I don’t know details but it shouldn’t be something too difficult."

447
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:09,000
Familiar voice: "And the pay will be good, enough for these raspberries and more."

448
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Virgil: "Is that so? Well... let me think about it."

449
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:15,000
*Should I take this offer? It might be a trap.*

450
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:26,000
*Also, they technically just asked me to get the raspberries, not to buy them. And I can tell this body is more agile than my own, so maybe I could put it to test.*

451
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:33,000
Narrator: "Virgil looks around, pondering his choices when a beggar approaches him asking him for gold."

452
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:38,000
Narrator: "He dismisses the man quickly, but this also gives him an idea."

453
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:45,000
*I could beg for the money that I need; is not too much anyhow, and it might be easier and safer.*

454
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:49,000
Virgil: "Alright, bring me to this acquaintance of yours."

455
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:51,000
Familiar voice: "Sure thing!"

456
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:52,000
*...*

457
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:59,000
*The man left in a hurry, just to come back a few minutes later, with a beautiful woman to his side.*

458
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:04,000
Familiar voice: "Here is the adventurer ma’am, you think he’s good enough?"

459
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:07,000
*Noblemwoman" "Mmmmh... It will suffice, now go.*

460
00:33:07,000 --> 00:33:09,000
Familiar voice: "Yes, ma’am!"

461
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:14,000
Familiar voice: "Now, I have a request for you. I need you to follow this man."

462
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Narrator: "The beautiful woman takes a piece of paper from her purse. On it, there is a drawing of an old man."

463
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Familiar voice: "Do you know him?"

464
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:25,000
Virgil: "No, I don’t think so."

465
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:39,000
Familiar voice: "Well, that doesn’t matters. I want you to follow him and tell me what he is doing. He is just a couple of blocks away in that direction. You should be going right now, or you’ll miss him."

466
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:43,000
Familiar voice: "And again, I want to know what he is up to!"

467
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:47,000
Virgil: "Wait, but we haven’t even talked about the terms."

468
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Familiar voice: "You’ll be well compensated, now go, don’t miss your chance!"

469
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:54,000
Virgil: "Ahh- Okay, fine!"

470
00:33:54,000 --> 00:34:01,000
Narrator: "Although he was not fully persuaded, the assertive woman pushed Virgil into doing her bidding."

471
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:04,000
*I-It’s not like that! I just want to be helpful!*

472
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:05,000
*......*

473
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,000
*...*

474
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:10,000
Narrator: "Virgil quickly catches up with the old man. "

475
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Narrator: "Although he can’t walk too fast due to his age, he is clearly in a hurry, and is trying to keep a low profile."

476
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:25,000
Narrator: "Still, our hero manages to keep his pace and distance, until he sees him going inside of a house."

477
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:32,000
Virgil: "I guess reporting that he arrived to this house won’t do much, but I should write down the address..."

478
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:40,000
Narrator: "Virgil hear noises coming from the house, and so he kept his distance for several minutes until they faded away."

479
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Narrator: "When he thought it was safe, he approached the window and looked inside; empty."

480
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:50,000
Virgil: "Well, I need to get in, but carefully. How, though?"

481
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:58,000
Narrator: "He silently stepped inside, and although he couldn’t see anyone, there was noise coming from the second floor."

482
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:01,000
*That sounds like someone is fucking...*

483
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:04,000
Narrator: "The noise led him to a a closed door."

484
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:09,000
Virgil: "Yeah, they definitely fucking, but will she just take my word for it?"

485
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:15,000
Narrator: "They weren’t big, nor intimidating, but he knew that they could bark at any moment."

486
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Virgil: "Shit, well, calm down buddy..."

487
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:22,000
Narrator: "As he said the words ‘calm down,’ the animal got angry."

488
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:24,000
Virgil: "Shit, okay, let me think..."

489
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:25,000
*......*

490
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:26,000
*...*

491
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:30,000
Narrator: "A few minutes later he was back at the market."

492
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:32,000
Virgil: "Shit, that was close..."

493
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:37,000
Narrator: "While he was grasping for air, the noblewoman approached him."

494
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Familiar voice: "Sweaty... I guess that means you got something done, right?"

495
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Virgil: "Yes! I followed him until he got inside of a house, this is the address..."

496
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Narrator: "Virgil hands her a paper, but she doesn’t reacts."

497
00:35:52,000 --> 00:36:00,000
Familiar voice: "I see, I don’t know this place. Definitely not one of his business. Did you found something else?"

498
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:04,000
Virgil: "Well, you see, he had ‘business’ there, but..."

499
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:09,000
Narrator: "He wasn’t sure about how to explain the encounter he just witnessed."

500
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:13,000
Virgil: "It was of the carnal kind, if you know what I mean?"

501
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:16,000
Familiar voice: "Are you sure of that?! "

502
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:21,000
Narrator: "The woman gave a purse with coins in it; with a value of a hundred."

503
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:29,000
Familiar voice: "I also talked with the merchant, he’ll hand you whatever you need, so this money is for yourself."

504
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:32,000
Virgil: "Ehh? Thank you a lot! Very kind. "

505
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:41,000
Familiar voice: "Yes, okay... Look, you have proved to be useful today, so perhaps I’ll hire you again. In the meantime, I have to go. "

506
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:44,000
Virgil: "Ah, yes! I’d gladly help again! Take care!"

507
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:52,000
Narrator: "The woman looks at him with curiosity; his behavior was odd, improper, but to her, that made him interesting."

508
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Familiar voice: "Okay."

509
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:58,000
Narrator: "With that said, she turned around and left."

510
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:04,000
Virgil: "Well, this worked better than I expected! Wait, she didn’t even give me her name..."

511
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:06,000
*This quest is a test, isn’t it?*

512
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:12,000
*I just need to figure out how to get the raspberries, not to actually waste my money on them.*

513
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:18,000
*What’d be the point of doing that? And that’s why my landlady also said she had no money.*

514
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:23,000
*Very well, it is settled them. I just need to come out with a plan.*

515
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:32,000
Narrator: "During the next few hours, Virgil would walk around the market, memorizing it and getting ready for his first grand heist."

516
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:38,000
Narrator: "Soon, he thought, it would get dark, and then it’d be the perfect time to strike."

517
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:49,000
Narrator: "As the merchants packed their goods and left, the only people that could be seen in this now deserted place were guards. And only a handful of them."

518
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:53,000
*Only a handful, uh? It seems like it is time to strike.*

519
00:37:53,000 --> 00:38:04,000
Narrator: "As Virgil used the shadows to hide himself, approaching to the tent that he knew had the sweet treasure needed for his errand, he noticed an outstanding guard."

520
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:11,000
Narrator: "He was at least 6’4, protected by heavy plates of armor, and a sword that could cut a horse in half."

521
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:24,000
Narrator: "He had no hair, but his thick mustache was white as snow; You could tell that he was a veteran that had fought over a hundred battles, a knight that once his mere presence inspired fear."

522
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:34,000
Narrator: "Virgil could only imagine how such a figure ended up here; was this, perhaps, a punishment? Or maybe he refused to be dismissed from the army?"

523
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:44,000
Narrator: "But the focus of our adventurer switched when he noticed the big pouch that was, undoubtedly, filled with gold coins, hanging on his side. "

524
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:50,000
Narrator: "Could he get close enough to grab it for himself? After all, he was already stealing."

525
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:53,000
*Mmmh... it’d be tricky, but I think I can do this.*

526
00:38:53,000 --> 00:38:57,000
*I should hurry to the tent now, I shouldn’t overstay my welcome.*

527
00:38:57,000 --> 00:39:02,000
Narrator: "Without further obstacles, Virgil arrived to the merchant’s cart."

528
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:09,000
Virgil: "Okay, I’m here now. Finding those raspberries will be easy, but perhaps I should look around..."

529
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:17,000
Narrator: "He examined the cart, and although there wasn’t much in it, he found a secret stash, with a small safe box in it."

530
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:21,000
Virgil: "A lock? There must be something valuable inside."

531
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:31,000
Narrator: "When Virgil arrived to this new world, he inspected his adventurer’s outfit, and he knew he had a lock pick in it, among other utility tools."

532
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:38,000
Virgil: "Do I have time for this? There weren’t many guards, but a patrol may arrive at any moment..."

533
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Virgil: "Open it will require some thief tools too..."

534
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:45,000
Virgil: "Need to hurry now, I haven’t-"

535
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:50,000
Narrator: "As he was planning to leave, he could see a patrol approaching."

536
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:53,000
Virgil: "Damn, too late! What now, let’s see..."

537
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:59,000
Narrator: "He inspected his surroundings, thinking about a route to quickly escape."

538
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Virgil: "If I can get to that roof, I can get away with without being noticed, other than that..."

539
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:16,000
Virgil: "I could run through those tents and carts; with the armors they have, it is unlikely they’ll be able to follow, but they definitely will see me go."

540
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:22,000
Narrator: "The group of men were getting close, it was time for Virgil to decide what to do."

541
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:26,000
*Stealing isn’t my style, and that merchant seems shady.*

542
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:30,000
*This may not be great, but it should honest work, right?*

543
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Narrator: "Virgil tried to convince himself that this was the best choice for him."

544
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:39,000
Virgil: "*sigh* Alright, let’s get to it. "

545
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:42,000
Virgil: "Sir, ma’am, a coin please?..."

546
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:48,000
Narrator: "He begged for a few hours until he got enough money to get the raspberries."

547
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:55,000
Narrator: "Thankfully none of his friends or acquaintances had seen him doing this humiliating task."

548
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:58,000
Narrator: "Or at least that’s what he believed."

549
00:40:58,000 --> 00:41:00,000
*Wait, someone did see me?*

550
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:03,000
Narrator: "No... not as far as you know."

551
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:08,000
**sigh* Well, at least I have everything with me now, time to go home...*

552
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:09,000
*......*

553
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:10,000
*...*

554
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:16,000
Narrator: "As Virgil arrives at his house, his eager landlady happily welcomed him."

555
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Sybil: "Darling! You came back!"

556
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:23,000
Virgil: "Ehh? Yeah, I mean I only had to get a few raspberries, you know?"

557
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:28,000
Sybil: "If you only knew how many people fail to do such a simple task."

558
00:41:28,000 --> 00:41:29,000
Virgil: "Do they?"

559
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Sybil: "Yeah, they can get frustrated with it and quit. Many adventurers don’t go past level one or two."

560
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:40,000
Virgil: "Wow, and I thought I had a lot of competition."

561
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:46,000
Sybil: "Well, don’t you worry, those who stay will probably be quite fierce in their progress."

562
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:49,000
Sybil: "Now, do you want to tell me how you did it?"

563
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:50,000
Virgil: "Heh, sure!"

564
00:41:50,000 --> 00:42:02,000
Sybil: "Anyhow, let’s have dinner so you can go and rest. This was but your first quest, but from now on, you will face bigger challenges, so you need to take care of yourself."

565
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:05,000
Virgil: "Yes, I’m as exhausted as I am hungry!."

566
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:08,000
Sybil: "Heh, alright, I prepared your favorite!"

567
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:10,000
Virgil: "Oh... yes, my favorite!"

568
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:16,000
Narrator: "Was Virgil expecting what he would call in his world a ‘burrito’? Probably not."

569
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:25,000
Narrator: "But even though it was similar, the fresh meat and ingredients used made the flavor and culinary experience a whole new thing."

570
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:32,000
Narrator: "When he was full, he barely could walk, and as soon as he got to his bed he fell asleep."

571
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:39,000
Narrator: "The hero got 30 gold as a reward, also earning 1 of fame, 0 of infamy, and 25 experience points. "

572
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:40,000
*......*

573
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:41,000
*...*

574
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:49,000
*The quest says that the goal is to get a flower in a mountain, but to go to the church first for further instructions.*

575
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:52,000
*Apparently, this is another retrieval quest.*

576
00:42:52,000 --> 00:43:02,000
*It seems like they don’t give you many choices when you are a level one adventurer, but I was hoping to go out and kill some monsters or something.*

577
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:04,000
Virgil: "Anyway, I should get going."

578
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:05,000
*......*

579
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:06,000
*...*

580
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Narrator: "As Virgil entered this holy place, he was marveled with it; the beautiful architecture, the smell of incense, and more than anything, the enormous statue that welcomed him."

581
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:30,000
Narrator: "He had no idea of what kind of God or Goddess is worshiped in this place, but he was certain that their devotion to them was strong, and for a moment, he felt humbled."

582
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:39,000
Narrator: "He was looking at the exquisite detail of the holy art that surrounded that he didn’t see the high priestess approaching."

583
00:43:39,000 --> 00:43:42,000
Familiar voice: "Welcome, adventurer."

584
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:45,000
Virgil: "My apologies! I didn’t mean to be rude!"

585
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:53,000
Familiar voice: "Don’t you worry, I can tell this is the first time you visit us. Although I have seen you around, Virgil."

586
00:43:53,000 --> 00:43:55,000
Virgil: "Oh? Have you?"

587
00:43:55,000 --> 00:44:04,000
Familiar voice: "Yes, you and your mother. She is quite a popular woman, although neither of you seem to be interested in Servilia’s wisdom."

588
00:44:04,000 --> 00:44:09,000
Virgil: "It's not that, it's just... I'm not acquainted with her philosophy."

589
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:17,000
Beatrice: "That’s fine; After all, you are not here as a devotee. Also, you can call me Priestess Beatrice, or just Beatrice."

590
00:44:17,000 --> 00:44:23,000
Narrator: "Virgil was surprised that she would allow him to refer her using her first name only."

591
00:44:23,000 --> 00:44:27,000
Beatrice: "And I assume you are here to help us, right?"

592
00:44:27,000 --> 00:44:30,000
Virgil: "Yes, something about collecting flowers?"

593
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:34,000
Beatrice: "If you put it that way, it sounds easy, doesn’t it?"

594
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:35,000
Virgil: "Yeah, kinda."

595
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:45,000
Beatrice: "Maybe you wonder why we don’t do it ourselves, but what happens is that we are preparing for a big celebration, and everyone here is quite busy."

596
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:53,000
Beatrice: "I’m sorry for not providing you with a particularly exciting adventure, but you’ll be well rewarded for your time."

597
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:58,000
Virgil: "Don’t worry! I don’t mind! So, I just need to know where to go."

598
00:44:58,000 --> 00:45:01,000
Beatrice: "Yes, let me give you the directions."

599
00:45:01,000 --> 00:45:10,000
Narrator: "Beatrice patiently explained to Virgil how to leave the city and what path to follow, so he could arrive to the Holy Valley."

600
00:45:10,000 --> 00:45:20,000
Beatrice: "I don’t think you can miss it. But remember, bring only one flower; they are sacred for us, and therefore we only use them in special occasions."

601
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:23,000
Virgil: "Okay, no problem with that. "

602
00:45:23,000 --> 00:45:25,000
Beatrice: "Take care, Virgil."

603
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:27,000
Virgil: "Thank you, priestess!"

604
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:28,000
*......*

605
00:45:28,000 --> 00:45:29,000
*...*

606
00:45:29,000 --> 00:45:33,000
Narrator: "The Virgil left the church, then the city."

607
00:45:33,000 --> 00:45:40,000
Narrator: "Thanks to Beatrice’s instructions, it was easy to find the right path through the forest."

608
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:47,000
Narrator: "The first hour of his journey was uneventful, but then, he found an old man walking back."

609
00:45:47,000 --> 00:45:52,000
Narrator: "He is bald, with a long beard and his skin tanned by the fierce sun."

610
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:59,000
Narrator: "Dressed in rags, the only possession that seemed dear to him was the staff he used to walk."

611
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:08,000
Narrator: "To Virgil's surprise, there is a flower decorating his walking tool. One with the same color as the one he needs to retrieve."

612
00:46:08,000 --> 00:46:12,000
*Mmmh, if he is coming from there, maybe I can ask him about it.*

613
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:14,000
Virgil: "Good day, good sir."

614
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:17,000
Familiar voice: "Good day indeed, son."

615
00:46:17,000 --> 00:46:20,000
Virgil: "Would you mind if I ask you a question?"

616
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:25,000
Narrator: "The elder didn’t seem bothered by the question, but he was struggling."

617
00:46:25,000 --> 00:46:28,000
Virgil: "Are you fine? Can I help you? "

618
00:46:28,000 --> 00:46:33,000
Familiar voice: "Oh, it’s nothing, don’t you worry about. What is your question?"

619
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:38,000
Virgil: "I’m just want to confirm if this is the path to the Holy Valley."

620
00:46:38,000 --> 00:46:43,000
Familiar voice: "So long your heart is in the right place, you can’t miss it."

621
00:46:43,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Virgil: "Ahhh... I’ll take that as a yes."

622
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:53,000
*He looks tired and hungry; his answer was cryptic, but I feel like I should do something about it.*

623
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:58,000
*Perhaps one of my rations with some water would help him in his journey.*

624
00:46:58,000 --> 00:46:59,000
*......*

625
00:46:59,000 --> 00:47:00,000
*...*

626
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:07,000
Narrator: "Virgil continued traveling, and as he approached his destination, he found an altar to Servilia’s."

627
00:47:07,000 --> 00:47:16,000
Narrator: "He barely knew anything about her or the church, but there was a prayer written on the wood, which helped him learn more about it."

628
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:25,000
Virgil: "O’ Goddess Servilia’s, wealthiest among them all, may this humble offer serve you well, so shall you bless us with your Golden Rain."

629
00:47:25,000 --> 00:47:31,000
Virgil: "Uhhh? Well, clearly ‘Golden Rain’ doesn’t means the same here than in my world."

630
00:47:31,000 --> 00:47:44,000
Narrator: "Curiously enough, he thought, the altar looked quite humble; it was built with wood and rocks, and it lacked decorations, except for a carving of a deer on it and a wooden box."

631
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:52,000
Virgil: "Nevertheless, there is a donation box. As I understand now, she must be the Goddess of prosperity and abundance."

632
00:47:52,000 --> 00:47:59,000
Narrator: "Virgil thought that if magic and other dimensions are real, maybe Gods and Goddesses are too."

633
00:47:59,000 --> 00:48:04,000
Narrator: "Is it worth it to give money to her, though? And how much, anyhow?"

634
00:48:04,000 --> 00:48:11,000
Narrator: "Virgil kneels at the altar and hopes for prosperity while he thanks the Goddess for her blessing."

635
00:48:11,000 --> 00:48:18,000
Narrator: "At the end, he doesn’t feels any change, but at least he feels more hopeful about the future."

636
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:21,000
*Time to continue, I shouldn’t be too far.*

637
00:48:21,000 --> 00:48:27,000
Narrator: "He was correct on his assessment; half an hour later, he was arriving to the valley."

638
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:33,000
Narrator: "The place was quiet and peaceful, and not a single soul but him in sight."

639
00:48:33,000 --> 00:48:37,000
Narrator: "And he felt at calm too... An eerie calm."

640
00:48:37,000 --> 00:48:44,000
Virgil: "Is there magic in this place? It doesn’t feels bad but... there is something here, for sure."

641
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:52,000
Narrator: "Virgil barely knew the house he was living in, let alone the many oddities that he will encounter in this world."

642
00:48:52,000 --> 00:48:58,000
Virgil: "Okay, that confirms it then; it is magic. But it must be good magic, right?"

643
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:02,000
Narrator: "He asked to himself, looking for reassurance."

644
00:49:02,000 --> 00:49:05,000
Virgil: "I guess I’ll have to figure it out."

645
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:10,000
Narrator: "The champion explored this new lands, looking for the valuable flower."

646
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:16,000
Narrator: "Finally, he noticed a mile away a big tree, and underneath it, a small flower field."

647
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:22,000
Narrator: "He hurried there, since he didn’t want to overextend his welcome in this location."

648
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:28,000
Narrator: "But when he was about to grab one, he heard a dangerous beast grunting behind him."

649
00:49:28,000 --> 00:49:33,000
Narrator: "It’s a buck, but a massive one, over 6 feet tall, and quite angry too."

650
00:49:33,000 --> 00:49:37,000
Virgil: "Shit! From where it came? I didn’t hear it coming."

651
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:47,000
Narrator: "Virgil only had a few seconds to think what to do; would he fight the beast? is there even a possibility for him to win against it?"

652
00:49:47,000 --> 00:49:57,000
Narrator: "He was really close to the big tree, and as far as he knew, deers can’t climb... but they jump, and very high too; is he fast enough?"

653
00:49:57,000 --> 00:50:04,000
Narrator: "Calming the beast seemed unlikely, but as unlikely as escaping the fury of this animal."

654
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:09,000
Narrator: "To Virgil’s surprise, it then turned around and left him alone."

655
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:11,000
Virgil: "Okay, that was weird."

656
00:50:11,000 --> 00:50:17,000
Narrator: "With a flower safe in Virgil’s bag, it was time for him to head back to the church."

657
00:50:17,000 --> 00:50:26,000
Narrator: "At first he was delighted by the valley, but now that had witness its protector, he just wanted to leave and avoid more trouble."

658
00:50:26,000 --> 00:50:27,000
*...*

659
00:50:27,000 --> 00:50:35,000
Narrator: "As he was about to arrive to the city, he felt that something was wrong; he was about to be ambushed!"

660
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:38,000
Virgil: "How the fuck do I know that, though?"

661
00:50:38,000 --> 00:50:43,000
Narrator: "He wasted his advantage in doing such a pointless question."

662
00:50:43,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Familiar voice: "Don’t move, stay right there!"

663
00:50:46,000 --> 00:50:52,000
Narrator: "The champion was startled, but that didn’t stop him from grabbing his weapon."

664
00:50:52,000 --> 00:50:54,000
Familiar voice: "What did I say?!"

665
00:50:54,000 --> 00:51:00,000
Narrator: "With inhuman swiftness, Virgil’s foe disarms him with a kick to his hand."

666
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:01,000
Virgil: "What th-"

667
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:08,000
Narrator: "Then, a voluptuous woman appears in front of him, not too happy by the trouble he was causing."

668
00:51:08,000 --> 00:51:20,000
Narrator: "It was a dark elf that the hero have never seen before, but he noticed her attire, which made him think she was an adventurer too, although not a new one like himself."

669
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:22,000
Virgil: "What do you want?!"

670
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:27,000
Familiar voice: "You are quite combative for a level one, aren’t you?"

671
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:30,000
Narrator: "Apparently, this attitude pleased her. "

672
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:37,000
Familiar voice: "But you know why I am here. Not like there could be that many reasons, aren’t they?"

673
00:51:37,000 --> 00:51:40,000
Virgil: "The flower? No way I’m giving it to you."

674
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:45,000
Familiar voice: "Look, calm down. Let’s make this easy for both of us."

675
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:52,000
Familiar voice: "But first, let me introduce myself. I’m Shael, and if I’m not wrong, you are Virgil."

676
00:51:52,000 --> 00:51:54,000
Virgil: "How do you know that?"

677
00:51:54,000 --> 00:52:00,000
Shael: "There is a ranking, and everyone is in there, even those at the bottom, like you."

678
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:09,000
Shael: "With that said, let us get to an agreement. I could just take the flower from you, and you wouldn’t be able to do anything about it."

679
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:16,000
Shael: "Or... what if you give it to me, and in exchange, I can show you my flower. And perhaps even more..."

680
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:17,000
Virgil: "Wait, what?"

681
00:52:17,000 --> 00:52:23,000
Shael: "It’d be easier and more exciting that way, don’t you think? It’s a win-win situation."

682
00:52:23,000 --> 00:52:24,000
Virgil: "I..."

683
00:52:24,000 --> 00:52:27,000
Narrator: "What will prevail? Reason or his lust?"

684
00:52:27,000 --> 00:52:30,000
Shael: "Now, let’s take what is mine."

685
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Narrator: "She kicked our brave hero again and made him roll, so she could access his pockets. "

686
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:43,000
Narrator: "Her expression changed when she realized that he have landed on the flower, crushing it."

687
00:52:43,000 --> 00:52:48,000
Shael: "Really?! Only one?! And did you just put it in there like that?!"

688
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:53,000
Shael: "It’s a delicate flower, this is not how you are supposed to handle it."

689
00:52:53,000 --> 00:52:56,000
Virgil: "I... I don’t know about that!"

690
00:52:56,000 --> 00:53:05,000
Shael: "*sigh* What a waste of time. At least I already got a bunch of them. Heck, even that old man was more competent than you."

691
00:53:05,000 --> 00:53:08,000
Shael: "Whatever, see you later, newbie."

692
00:53:08,000 --> 00:53:15,000
Narrator: "It took our hero a few minutes to recover, and felt sadden when he realized what have happened."

693
00:53:15,000 --> 00:53:21,000
Virgil: "Shit, not strong enough even to protect a flower... I really need to train more."

694
00:53:21,000 --> 00:53:24,000
Narrator: "He looked at the crushed flower."

695
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:28,000
Virgil: "*sigh* I wonder if they’ll accept my explanation."

696
00:53:28,000 --> 00:53:36,000
Narrator: "He got up and walked back to town, hoping that at least they wouldn’t punish him too hard for failing."

697
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:37,000
*......*

698
00:53:37,000 --> 00:53:38,000
*...*

699
00:53:38,000 --> 00:53:43,000
Narrator: "As he entered the holy temple, Virgil felt his heart shrink."

700
00:53:43,000 --> 00:53:48,000
Narrator: "The flower was crushed, as was his hope to accomplish this quest."

701
00:53:48,000 --> 00:53:56,000
Narrator: "Not just that, but the dark elf that he just met was delivering flowers; giving Beatrice many at once."

702
00:53:56,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Narrator: "Virgil expected the priestess to be angry, since the quest said to only pick one, but instead the holy woman seemed pleased at her."

703
00:54:06,000 --> 00:54:13,000
Narrator: "After the thief received a generous reward, she turned around and walked towards you, smiling."

704
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:19,000
Shael: "You came after all? You may be as brave as you are a degenerate, aren’t you?"

705
00:54:19,000 --> 00:54:23,000
Shael: "Good luck with that withering flower of yours, hah."

706
00:54:23,000 --> 00:54:28,000
Narrator: "After mocking Virgil one last time, she left the building."

707
00:54:28,000 --> 00:54:39,000
Narrator: "Now it was time for him to talk with Beatrice, and as he approaches her, he notices the smile on her face; at least she’s in a good mood, he thought."

708
00:54:39,000 --> 00:54:42,000
Beatrice: "Welcome back, Virgil. Any good news?"

709
00:54:42,000 --> 00:54:45,000
Virgil: "Hello Beatrice. Er- Well, I do have news."

710
00:54:45,000 --> 00:54:47,000
Beatrice: "Are you alright?"

711
00:54:47,000 --> 00:54:50,000
Narrator: "She noticed something was off."

712
00:54:50,000 --> 00:54:57,000
Virgil: "Yes, I’m fine I think, but... Let us say that I had to face some unexpected challenges on my way here."

713
00:54:57,000 --> 00:54:59,000
Beatrice: "Is that so?"

714
00:54:59,000 --> 00:55:03,000
Virgil: "Yes, in fact... It’s better to show than to tell."

715
00:55:03,000 --> 00:55:07,000
Narrator: "Virgil takes out the flower from his pocket."

716
00:55:07,000 --> 00:55:11,000
Narrator: "The priestess expression changes to one of sadness."

717
00:55:11,000 --> 00:55:15,000
Beatrice: "I see... Do you want to tell me what happened?"

718
00:55:15,000 --> 00:55:22,000
Virgil: "Yes, well, I was assaulted on my way back, and during the fight I ended up falling on top of it."

719
00:55:22,000 --> 00:55:28,000
Virgil: "I apologize for my failure, and accept full responsibility for what happened."

720
00:55:28,000 --> 00:55:35,000
Narrator: "He thinks he is about to be scolded, so he is surprised when she sees her smiling again."

721
00:55:35,000 --> 00:55:43,000
Narrator: "She gives to our hero a pouch with 30 gold in exchange of the flower, also earning 1 fame point and 20 experience. "

722
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:51,000
Narrator: "Once she had fulfilled her part of the contract, her expression changed again to one of utter seriousness."

723
00:55:51,000 --> 00:55:58,000
Beatrice: "But, even though we decided to be generous this time, you need to understand a few things."

724
00:55:58,000 --> 00:55:59,000
Virgil: "Sure ma’am!"

725
00:55:59,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Beatrice: "Sometimes quests are very straightforward; do what you are asked and everything will be fine."

726
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:17,000
Beatrice: "But in other occasions, things will not be as clear cut; we are the church of abundance, and therefore we always aim to get more than the bare minimum."

727
00:56:17,000 --> 00:56:18,000
Virgil: "But the-"

728
00:56:18,000 --> 00:56:29,000
Beatrice: "Yes, indeed it says that, but sometimes the real needs of your patrons may differ, and if you are capable of seeing that, you might accomplish more."

729
00:56:29,000 --> 00:56:37,000
Beatrice: "Indeed it is a risk to deviate from what has been written, but the rewards may also be noticeably more hefty."

730
00:56:37,000 --> 00:56:46,000
Beatrice: "I mention it because you are new, and this might help you in your future ventures; don’t box yourself with a few vague requests."

731
00:56:46,000 --> 00:56:50,000
Virgil: "Thank you! That’s good to know! I appreciate your wisdom!"

732
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:56,000
Beatrice: "Well then, now you can go back home with something more valuable than money."

733
00:56:56,000 --> 00:56:59,000
Virgil: "I will, a pleasure to meet you."

734
00:56:59,000 --> 00:57:01,000
Beatrice: "See you around, kiddo."

735
00:57:01,000 --> 00:57:08,000
Narrator: "Virgil left the church happy and went back home after miraculously succeeding in his first quest."

736
00:57:08,000 --> 00:57:16,000
Narrator: "Granted, they were being kind to him, but still, it was the first of the many adventures that he still has ahead..."

737
00:57:16,000 --> 00:57:17,000
*......*

738
00:57:17,000 --> 00:57:18,000
*...*

739
00:57:18,000 --> 00:57:21,000
Virgil: "Alright, let's see what can I do toda-"

740
00:57:21,000 --> 00:57:22,000
Laia: "Hi, Virgil!"

741
00:57:22,000 --> 00:57:24,000
Virgil: "Oh, hey, what's up?"

742
00:57:24,000 --> 00:57:27,000
Laia: "Are you busy? Did you already pick a quest?"

743
00:57:27,000 --> 00:57:29,000
Virgil: "Not really, was about to."

744
00:57:29,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Laia: "Great! You see, there is a quest I want to do, but it requires two people, and I was wondering..."

745
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:38,000
Virgil: "Sure, I'll help you out!"

746
00:57:38,000 --> 00:57:41,000
Laia: "Thanks! I knew I could count on you."

747
00:57:41,000 --> 00:57:42,000
Virgil: "Which one?"

748
00:57:42,000 --> 00:57:43,000
Laia: "That one."

749
00:57:43,000 --> 00:57:56,000
Narrator: "She points to a low-level quest that barely gives any gold or experience, at least compared to quest with the same difficulty, which makes Virgil wonder why she'd be so interested in it."

750
00:57:56,000 --> 00:57:58,000
Virgil: "This one? are you sure?"

751
00:57:58,000 --> 00:58:01,000
Laia: "Yes, you see, there is an extra reward."

752
00:58:01,000 --> 00:58:04,000
Virgil: "A 'Crystalic Sun'? What's that?"

753
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:09,000
Laia: "It's a special crystal that can be used for... a few things. "

754
00:58:09,000 --> 00:58:17,000
Laia: "It is somewhat expensive and rare, and since not many people use it, it's hard to sell or find in stores."

755
00:58:17,000 --> 00:58:22,000
Laia: "You can keep the money; I just need the crystal for... reasons."

756
00:58:22,000 --> 00:58:27,000
Virgil: "Sure, you can keep it. And I'm curious about doing a quest like this."

757
00:58:27,000 --> 00:58:30,000
Laia: "Okay, let's party up, and let's go!"

758
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:35,000
Laia: "Alright, we need to retrieve a missing object for this quest."

759
00:58:35,000 --> 00:58:36,000
Virgil: "Again?"

760
00:58:36,000 --> 00:58:39,000
Laia: "We are level one, so what do you expect?"

761
00:58:39,000 --> 00:58:43,000
Virgil: "*sigh* At least we are close to quest  already."

762
00:58:43,000 --> 00:58:47,000
Laia: "Yep! But don't expect to be slaying dragons any time soon!"

763
00:58:47,000 --> 00:58:51,000
Virgil: "Come on, Laia, don't kill the dream. Let's go now."

764
00:58:51,000 --> 00:58:53,000
Laia: "Okay, take the lead!"

765
00:58:53,000 --> 00:59:01,000
Narrator: "Following the quest indications, the pair follow a road for a few hours until they arrive at a field."

766
00:59:01,000 --> 00:59:09,000
Narrator: "There, they are surprised to find not a town, but a community of what Virgil would describe as 'Hippies.'"

767
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:17,000
Narrator: "But before they approach them, they find something perturbing; the remains of many previous adventurers. "

768
00:59:17,000 --> 00:59:23,000
Narrator: "Most of them have turned into skeletons already, but a few had dried out."

769
00:59:23,000 --> 00:59:26,000
Laia: "I-Is... is this what I think it is?!"

770
00:59:26,000 --> 00:59:28,000
Virgil: "Yeah, these are corpses..."

771
00:59:28,000 --> 00:59:34,000
Narrator: "Just a few feet away from them, there was a sign that said 'Welcome to ShowSkin!'"

772
00:59:34,000 --> 00:59:37,000
Virgil: "What does this even mean?..."

773
00:59:37,000 --> 00:59:42,000
Laia: "This is really dangerous; what should we do? Should we quit?"

774
00:59:42,000 --> 00:59:47,000
Narrator: "The nervous newbie was scared, but Virgil wouldn't give up as easily."

775
00:59:47,000 --> 00:59:51,000
Narrator: "He looked around, looking for clues of what happened."

776
00:59:51,000 --> 00:59:55,000
Narrator: "Then, finally, he realized a crucial detail."

777
00:59:55,000 --> 00:59:56,000
Virgil: "Naked!"

778
00:59:56,000 --> 00:59:57,000
Laia: "What?!"

779
00:59:57,000 --> 01:00:03,000
Virgil: "Look, those hippies are naked, and these bodies, their clothes are all torn apart."

780
01:00:03,000 --> 01:00:05,000
Laia: "What is a hippie?"

781
01:00:05,000 --> 01:00:09,000
Virgil: "Ehh? Nothing, just... Look, I have an idea. "

782
01:00:09,000 --> 01:00:12,000
Laia: "Mmmh... I have a bad feeling about this. "

783
01:00:12,000 --> 01:00:16,000
Virgil: "I bet we can get inside if we just get naked."

784
01:00:16,000 --> 01:00:20,000
Laia: "Naked?! No way, you are crazy! There must be another way!"

785
01:00:20,000 --> 01:00:27,000
Narrator: "Virgil paused and thought for a few minutes; maybe there was a loophole he could exploit."

786
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:29,000
Virgil: "Yes! There is another way! "

787
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:33,000
Laia: "Really? I thought you were going... Okay, I'm listening."

788
01:00:33,000 --> 01:00:43,000
Virgil: "Yeah, you see... it’s named 'ShowSkin,' it doesn't have to be our own, you know... And it is not like our friends here need theirs anymore."

789
01:00:43,000 --> 01:00:46,000
Laia: "You can't be serious, aren't you?"

790
01:00:46,000 --> 01:00:48,000
Virgil: "Do you have any idea?"

791
01:00:48,000 --> 01:00:50,000
Laia: "*sigh* Not really."

792
01:00:50,000 --> 01:00:56,000
Virgil: "Well, perhaps it'd be better to just quit; it is not like the reward is worth it."

793
01:00:56,000 --> 01:00:59,000
Laia: "No, wait. We should try, but... "

794
01:00:59,000 --> 01:01:03,000
Narrator: "Laia felt hopeless, but she truly wanted the crystal."

795
01:01:03,000 --> 01:01:10,000
Laia: "You are the party leader, so it is up to you; pick what we should do, and I'll stick to the plan. "

796
01:01:10,000 --> 01:01:14,000
Virgil: "Okay, this doesn't make it easier for me, but..."

797
01:01:14,000 --> 01:01:21,000
Narrator: "Virgil was thinking about how people would react if they knew what he was about to do. "

798
01:01:21,000 --> 01:01:32,000
Narrator: "He concluded that going naked would be the least problematic choice; there was no way that using someone's skin as an outfit would be considered acceptable."

799
01:01:32,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Narrator: "And yet, that would at least spare Laia of the shame and humiliation of being naked in front of you, and a bunch of likely old perverts."

800
01:01:42,000 --> 01:01:49,000
Narrator: "Our heroes cautiously entered the community, but lucky for them, no one cared about their presence."

801
01:01:49,000 --> 01:01:57,000
Narrator: "As Virgil suspected, most were old men, but there was enough in age, gender, and races to make it interesting."

802
01:01:57,000 --> 01:02:08,000
Narrator: "He also noticed that these were not just regular people, but many of them were using magic; a surprising fact considering how few users supposedly are."

803
01:02:08,000 --> 01:02:14,000
*I wonder what attracts them to this place; even the Holy Valley felt more special than here.*

804
01:02:14,000 --> 01:02:21,000
Narrator: "While our champion was rambling to himself, his partner was actively looking for the artifact."

805
01:02:21,000 --> 01:02:26,000
Laia: "*Sigh* I don't see any lamp around, of any kind for that matter..."

806
01:02:26,000 --> 01:02:28,000
Virgil: "Yeah, me neither!"

807
01:02:28,000 --> 01:02:31,000
Virgil: "Ehh... Do you think we should ask around? "

808
01:02:31,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Laia: "With them?! But, they all look... suspicious, don't you think?"

809
01:02:36,000 --> 01:02:41,000
Laia: "And I'm pretty sure every single one of them is smoking something weird."

810
01:02:41,000 --> 01:02:47,000
Virgil: "Perhaps, but if what we are looking it's someone's treasure, it will likely be hidden."

811
01:02:47,000 --> 01:02:52,000
Laia: "Yeah, you are right. We need to ask around. But let's stick together."

812
01:02:52,000 --> 01:02:55,000
Virgil: "Don't worry, I won't leave you alone."

813
01:02:55,000 --> 01:03:02,000
Narrator: "The two of them tried to act naturally; approaching small groups and trying to mingle with them."

814
01:03:02,000 --> 01:03:09,000
Narrator: "It was clear they all could sense Laia's magic since they asked about her healing powers. "

815
01:03:09,000 --> 01:03:15,000
Narrator: "But something was puzzling about Virgil, and none of them knew exactly what was it."

816
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:20,000
Narrator: "Nevertheless, no one seemed to stop them or bother them for too long."

817
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:29,000
Narrator: "After a while, they finally found a clue; a small group was gathered around a fire, grilling meat, drinking, and smoking."

818
01:03:29,000 --> 01:03:33,000
Narrator: "When they asked about the lamp, one of them laughed."

819
01:03:33,000 --> 01:03:37,000
Familiar voice: 1 "A lamp? Oh yes, I know who has one of those!"

820
01:03:37,000 --> 01:03:38,000
Laia: "You do?!"

821
01:03:38,000 --> 01:03:42,000
Virgil: "Can you tell us? We want to... talk with them!"

822
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:45,000
Familiar voice: 1 "I sure could! But..."

823
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:46,000
Virgil: "But?"

824
01:03:46,000 --> 01:03:54,000
Familiar voice: 1 "You two don't seem to be having fun; Join us for a while, smoke a little. Don't be party poopers..."

825
01:03:54,000 --> 01:03:56,000
Laia: "No way! I... We... "

826
01:03:56,000 --> 01:04:05,000
Narrator: "She turned around, looking at Virgil; was it wise to piss them off? What if they kicked you from the community, or worse?"

827
01:04:05,000 --> 01:04:14,000
Narrator: "But they don't know what could happen if they joined them, and Virgil suspected they have more in mind than just chatting..."

828
01:04:14,000 --> 01:04:18,000
*For him to be calling someone 'old,' it has to be pretty ancient!*

829
01:04:18,000 --> 01:04:20,000
Virgil: "Yeah, he has it?"

830
01:04:20,000 --> 01:04:28,000
Familiar voice: 1 "Yep! But mind you, it is his favorite pipe, so he might be reluctant to even show it off to you."

831
01:04:28,000 --> 01:04:31,000
Laia: "That's okay, we can deal with that. "

832
01:04:31,000 --> 01:04:36,000
Familiar voice: 1 "If you say so, good luck, you two, and take care!"

833
01:04:36,000 --> 01:04:39,000
Virgil: "Finally, time to finish our search..."

834
01:04:39,000 --> 01:04:44,000
Narrator: "When our champions arrived with the old man, he greeted them."

835
01:04:44,000 --> 01:04:49,000
Familiar voice: "Welcome, Virgil and Laia. I suppose you are here for this."

836
01:04:49,000 --> 01:04:53,000
Narrator: "He opened one of his bags and took out a lamp."

837
01:04:53,000 --> 01:04:54,000
Laia: "How-"

838
01:04:54,000 --> 01:04:58,000
Familiar voice: "Heh, my power goes beyond some basic divination. "

839
01:04:58,000 --> 01:05:07,000
Familiar voice: "With that said... I'm getting too old for these things; What was your plan? To convince me? Fight me? Deceive me? "

840
01:05:07,000 --> 01:05:17,000
Familiar voice: "Either way, it'd be a waste of time for both of us, and to tell you the truth, I have no more use for this artifact, so take it."

841
01:05:17,000 --> 01:05:19,000
Virgil: "Are you sure about that?"

842
01:05:19,000 --> 01:05:22,000
Laia: "We can compensate you for it, or-"

843
01:05:22,000 --> 01:05:29,000
Familiar voice: "It's fine, it's fine. You already went through a lot; Just take it, and let's enjoy our day."

844
01:05:29,000 --> 01:05:32,000
Laia: "Okay, well... thank you a lot, mister!"

845
01:05:32,000 --> 01:05:34,000
Virgil: "Yeah, very appreciated!"

846
01:05:34,000 --> 01:05:39,000
Familiar voice: "Oh boy, you don't know how much you will be. Now, let me be."

847
01:05:39,000 --> 01:05:45,000
Narrator: "Since they didn't want to displease such a helpful soul, they walked away."

848
01:05:45,000 --> 01:05:54,000
Narrator: "Once outside of the community, when the two of them were about to dress in their normal outfits, they saw someone arriving."

849
01:05:54,000 --> 01:05:59,000
Narrator: "She was short, green, and was dressed like a thief; a goblin no doubt."

850
01:05:59,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Narrator: "She was riding a cart loaded with boxes; you suspected she was the dealer that supplied this place."

851
01:06:06,000 --> 01:06:16,000
Narrator: "Although both Virgil and Laia ignored her, she was curious about the adventurers that managed to come out alive from such a dangerous place."

852
01:06:16,000 --> 01:06:19,000
Familiar voice: "Howdy, friends. Leaving already?"

853
01:06:19,000 --> 01:06:25,000
Laia: "She acts friendly, but I don't trust her, Virgil. Don't trust anyone here..."

854
01:06:25,000 --> 01:06:27,000
Narrator: "Her friend whispered."

855
01:06:27,000 --> 01:06:30,000
Virgil: "Hello! Yeah, we were just visiting..."

856
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:35,000
Familiar voice: "Visiting, uh? People don't just visit this place, you know..."

857
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:38,000
Laia: "Yeah, well, we are in a hurry, so..."

858
01:06:38,000 --> 01:06:41,000
Familiar voice: "And what's that? An old lamp?"

859
01:06:41,000 --> 01:06:43,000
Virgil: "Ehh? No, it's, erm..."

860
01:06:43,000 --> 01:06:54,000
Narrator: "The goblin had sharp eyes, and Virgil stumbled for a moment; should he try to deceive her? Or, at this point, maybe some honesty would be the way out?"

861
01:06:54,000 --> 01:07:04,000
Narrator: "The goblin got down from her cart and approached. Both adventurers got their guard up, but the goblin didn't seem to be looking for trouble."

862
01:07:04,000 --> 01:07:07,000
Jay: "I'm Jay; it's a pleasure to meet you both."

863
01:07:07,000 --> 01:07:09,000
Virgil: "Ehh... I'm Virgil."

864
01:07:09,000 --> 01:07:10,000
Laia: "Mmmh... Laia."

865
01:07:10,000 --> 01:07:16,000
Narrator: "Our heroes hesitated; they didn't know what to do in a situation like this."

866
01:07:16,000 --> 01:07:21,000
Narrator: "Jay got back on her cart, and soon her horses were walking again."

867
01:07:21,000 --> 01:07:23,000
Virgil: "That was weird..."

868
01:07:23,000 --> 01:07:27,000
Laia: "Yeah... I don't think you should take any job from her."

869
01:07:27,000 --> 01:07:31,000
Virgil: "You are right; it's probably a bad idea. Let's go now."

870
01:07:31,000 --> 01:07:34,000
Laia: "Yeah, or we might find another weirdo..."

871
01:07:34,000 --> 01:07:35,000
*......*

872
01:07:35,000 --> 01:07:36,000
*...*

873
01:07:36,000 --> 01:07:38,000
Narrator: "Back at the city..."

874
01:07:38,000 --> 01:07:43,000
Laia: "Heh, now let's deliver this; I really want my Crystalic Sun!"

875
01:07:43,000 --> 01:07:46,000
Virgil: "Sure, we are just a couple of blocks away."

876
01:07:46,000 --> 01:07:51,000
Narrator: "As they arrive at their destination, an old woman receives them. "

877
01:07:51,000 --> 01:07:56,000
Familiar voice: "Oh, you kids are the brave adventurers that took my quest?"

878
01:07:56,000 --> 01:07:58,000
Laia: "Yes, we are, ma'am."

879
01:07:58,000 --> 01:08:02,000
Virgil: "We did our best to be as swift as possible."

880
01:08:02,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Narrator: "Virgil takes out the lamp and gives it to her."

881
01:08:06,000 --> 01:08:16,000
Familiar voice: "Thank you, thank you a lot! You see, this is a family inheritance, but someone stole it from me many years ago, a wizard that..."

882
01:08:16,000 --> 01:08:23,000
Narrator: "The woman talks and talks about her past, to the point that even Laia's patience was being tested."

883
01:08:23,000 --> 01:08:32,000
Familiar voice: "Anyhow, I guess I should go for your reward, but you see, I'm pretty old, so could you help me out, young man? "

884
01:08:32,000 --> 01:08:33,000
Virgil: "No problem!"

885
01:08:33,000 --> 01:08:38,000
Familiar voice: "Thank you again, and you can wait here... Laia, you said?"

886
01:08:38,000 --> 01:08:41,000
Laia: "Yes! And don't worry about me."

887
01:08:41,000 --> 01:08:44,000
Familiar voice: "You are such a sweetheart."

888
01:08:44,000 --> 01:08:49,000
Narrator: "As they enter the house, Virgil feels that something isn't right."

889
01:08:49,000 --> 01:09:00,000
Narrator: "He can't tell exactly what's wrong, but there is just something in the air, and when the old woman perceives Virgil's reaction, her demeanor changes."

890
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:03,000
Familiar voice: "Oh? Excellent instincts."

891
01:09:03,000 --> 01:09:05,000
Virgil: "What are you up to?"

892
01:09:05,000 --> 01:09:10,000
Narrator: "He tried to grab his weapon, but to his surprise, it had vanished."

893
01:09:10,000 --> 01:09:17,000
Familiar voice: "What I am up to? It'd take me more than your entire lifespan to explain that to you."

894
01:09:17,000 --> 01:09:19,000
Virgil: "Are you a demon?!"

895
01:09:19,000 --> 01:09:27,000
Familiar voice: "A demon? Don't insult me like that... But I'll have to show myself; otherwise, you'll never understand."

896
01:09:27,000 --> 01:09:30,000
Narrator: "The room turned white, and then..."

897
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:32,000
Virgil: "Oh, what the f..."

898
01:09:32,000 --> 01:09:34,000
Familiar voice: "Exactly! Surprised?"

899
01:09:34,000 --> 01:09:38,000
Virgil: "Ehh... I still have no clue of what you are."

900
01:09:38,000 --> 01:09:48,000
Familiar voice: "What do you mean by that? I'm sure you have Djinns in your world. Although you look young, so perhaps you know us as 'Genies.' "

901
01:09:48,000 --> 01:09:53,000
Familiar voice: "Heck, you even had to bring me my lamp, you know..."

902
01:09:53,000 --> 01:09:59,000
Virgil: "Oh, yeah, I guess you are right... Wait, how did you know about the other world?"

903
01:09:59,000 --> 01:10:03,000
Familiar voice: "Heh, for someone like me, it's plain as day."

904
01:10:03,000 --> 01:10:09,000
Virgil: "A Djinn, you said, right?... Wait, does that means I'll get 3 wishes too?"

905
01:10:09,000 --> 01:10:13,000
Familiar voice: "Are you sure you want 3 wishes from me?"

906
01:10:13,000 --> 01:10:14,000
Virgil: "Ehh..."

907
01:10:14,000 --> 01:10:19,000
Tamara: "Anyway, my name is Tamara, the Whimsical Queen of Mischief and Delight."

908
01:10:19,000 --> 01:10:21,000
Virgil: "A pleasure, I'm Virgil."

909
01:10:21,000 --> 01:10:24,000
Tamara: "You already told me your name before..."

910
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:25,000
Virgil: "Ah, true..."

911
01:10:25,000 --> 01:10:27,000
Virgil: "So, what happens now?"

912
01:10:27,000 --> 01:10:28,000
Tamara: "About what?"

913
01:10:28,000 --> 01:10:32,000
Virgil: "Well, do I get something for getting your lamp?"

914
01:10:32,000 --> 01:10:36,000
Tamara: "Yeah, 50 gold coins, experience, and a Crystalic sun."

915
01:10:36,000 --> 01:10:39,000
Virgil: "Oh, okay, I guess that's fair..."

916
01:10:39,000 --> 01:10:44,000
Tamara: "I'm just kidding; let me explain to you what happened, but first."

917
01:10:44,000 --> 01:10:51,000
Narrator: "She snaps her fingers, and Virgil notices that movement outside the house has stopped."

918
01:10:51,000 --> 01:10:56,000
Tamara: "This might take a while, and I don't want your friend to interrupt us."

919
01:10:56,000 --> 01:10:58,000
Virgil: "Wow, that's cool! "

920
01:10:58,000 --> 01:11:07,000
Tamara: "You see, that old wizard took my lamp a few centuries ago. The bastard was using it like a fucking pipe, can you believe it?"

921
01:11:07,000 --> 01:11:13,000
Virgil: "Oh yeah, we noticed. You probably want to clean it up thoroughly before getting inside."

922
01:11:13,000 --> 01:11:16,000
Tamara: "I don't even want to think about that. "

923
01:11:16,000 --> 01:11:20,000
Tamara: "What he did was not a coincidence nor a random whim. "

924
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:29,000
Tamara: "He has slowly been absorbing its magic all this time, and now that it has been pretty much depleted, it is but scrap to him."

925
01:11:29,000 --> 01:11:33,000
Virgil: "Does that means that you are powerless now?"

926
01:11:33,000 --> 01:11:40,000
Tamara: "Not quite, but don't expect me to do any reality-bending magic for a couple of centuries."

927
01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:46,000
Virgil: "Okay, I think I get the picture now. You want to get your powers back and-"

928
01:11:46,000 --> 01:11:51,000
Tamara: "No, that's not how it works. I'll just have to let it recharge. "

929
01:11:51,000 --> 01:12:03,000
Tamara: "In the meantime, I already spent a lot of time pretending to be an old woman; I want to have fun, but I also need to keep a low profile, and that's where you come to mind."

930
01:12:03,000 --> 01:12:04,000
Virgil: "Me? Why?"

931
01:12:04,000 --> 01:12:15,000
Tamara: "Well, to begin with, you managed to finish this quest in one piece; I've sent over a dozen adventurers, and I'm sure you met the few that left bodies behind."

932
01:12:15,000 --> 01:12:23,000
Tamara: "Also, you are... creative. None of them ever thought about doing what you did, and that alone makes you interesting."

933
01:12:23,000 --> 01:12:34,000
Tamara: "And lastly, there is something special about you... not just the fact that you come from another world, but there is magic inside you, a special kind of it too."

934
01:12:34,000 --> 01:12:36,000
Virgil: "Special magic? How?"

935
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:45,000
Tamara: "Look, I don't want to give you a full course of how magic works in this world; you need to figure or find that out on your own."

936
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:50,000
Tamara: "I can tell you that there are only a few types of magic here. "

937
01:12:50,000 --> 01:13:00,000
Tamara: "For example, white magic heals and cures people, among other valuable tricks. Destruction magic... well, that one is self-explanatory, I hope. "

938
01:13:00,000 --> 01:13:05,000
Tamara: "But yours, although still dormant, it's really rare. Almost unique."

939
01:13:05,000 --> 01:13:09,000
Virgil: "That's intriguing! So what is what I can do?"

940
01:13:09,000 --> 01:13:15,000
Tamara: "Yours is the magic of temptation; the ability to create and raise people's desire."

941
01:13:15,000 --> 01:13:22,000
Tamara: "With enough practice, you'll be able to shape people's wants and use that to your advantage."

942
01:13:22,000 --> 01:13:31,000
Tamara: "You might not be able to destroy a building on a whim, but if you are savvy, you'll control kings and wizards to do that for you."

943
01:13:31,000 --> 01:13:38,000
Tamara: "But beware;  one of the reasons that this magic is so scarce it's because its users are hunted down. "

944
01:13:38,000 --> 01:13:43,000
Tamara: "After all, this is also one of the biggest threats this place can face."

945
01:13:43,000 --> 01:13:46,000
Virgil: "Auch, sounds like a curse in disguise."

946
01:13:46,000 --> 01:13:54,000
Tamara: "That'd be up to you; If you go around turning everyone into mindless bimbos, they'll catch you very quickly."

947
01:13:54,000 --> 01:13:58,000
Tamara: "But this magic can be as subtle as you want it to be."

948
01:13:58,000 --> 01:14:04,000
Virgil: "Okay, that's nice, but... you know I can't actually do anything, though? "

949
01:14:04,000 --> 01:14:12,000
Virgil: "And as far as I can tell, it'd take me years just to learn the basics, so how is this knowledge useful?"

950
01:14:12,000 --> 01:14:15,000
Tamara: "That's been the case... until now!"

951
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:22,000
Narrator: "A blinding light fills the room, and Virgil can't help it but to cover his face and close his eyes."

952
01:14:22,000 --> 01:14:30,000
Narrator: "He also feels something burning deep inside of him; his very soul was being awakened with the help of the Djinn."

953
01:14:30,000 --> 01:14:33,000
Tamara: "Heh, tell me, how do you feel now?"

954
01:14:33,000 --> 01:14:36,000
Virgil: "Weird, I don't know, really."

955
01:14:36,000 --> 01:14:42,000
Tamara: "Don't worry, I'll be helping you for a few days to make up for years of training. "

956
01:14:42,000 --> 01:14:46,000
Tamara: "Oh, and also, I'll be staying with you from now on."

957
01:14:46,000 --> 01:14:53,000
Virgil: "Wait, I can't explain to my household why a big-titted naked blue girl is living with me!"

958
01:14:53,000 --> 01:14:57,000
Tamara: "Do you call this big-titted? Don't make me laugh."

959
01:14:57,000 --> 01:15:02,000
Narrator: "Virgil witness how the Djinn's breast grew significantly in size."

960
01:15:02,000 --> 01:15:07,000
Virgil: "Wow! Those are impressive! How can you even walk with them?!"

961
01:15:07,000 --> 01:15:15,000
Tamara: "I can see that you like them. Maybe I should keep my original size and keep these changes for a future incentive."

962
01:15:15,000 --> 01:15:16,000
Virgil: "Ohhh..."

963
01:15:16,000 --> 01:15:25,000
Tamara: "Also, don't worry, I can turn invisible. And even though it's annoying, I can share that headspace that your narrator has."

964
01:15:25,000 --> 01:15:27,000
Narrator: "Wait, don't get in here!"

965
01:15:27,000 --> 01:15:28,000
Tamara: "Too late!"

966
01:15:28,000 --> 01:15:30,000
Narrator: "Come on, you are too big!"

967
01:15:30,000 --> 01:15:34,000
Tamara: "You already know I can get way bigger, so..."

968
01:15:34,000 --> 01:15:37,000
Virgil: "Come on, let's keep it in peace."

969
01:15:37,000 --> 01:15:42,000
Tamara: "Fine. Still, don't worry about talking with me; no one will notice."

970
01:15:42,000 --> 01:15:49,000
Virgil: "Okay, that's convenient... I guess if it's going to work like that, you can stay with me. "

971
01:15:49,000 --> 01:15:55,000
Tamara: "Good! But let's be honest; you would have figured out a way to get me there anyway."

972
01:15:55,000 --> 01:16:03,000
Tamara: "For now, let's try your powers, shall we? Take the Crystalic sun with you, and I'll tell you what to do."

973
01:16:03,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Virgil: "Mmmh... Kinda have a bad feeling about it."

974
01:16:06,000 --> 01:16:08,000
Tamara: "More like a boner."

975
01:16:08,000 --> 01:16:10,000
Narrator: "Yeah, totally a boner."

976
01:16:10,000 --> 01:16:11,000
*......*

977
01:16:11,000 --> 01:16:12,000
*...*

978
01:16:12,000 --> 01:16:17,000
Narrator: "After a few moments to calm down, Virgil asked Laia to come inside."

979
01:16:17,000 --> 01:16:19,000
Laia: "Hey, where is the old woman?"

980
01:16:19,000 --> 01:16:22,000
Virgil: "She had to go, but she gave me this."

981
01:16:22,000 --> 01:16:24,000
Laia: "The Crystalic sun!"

982
01:16:24,000 --> 01:16:27,000
Virgil: "This is what you wanted, right?"

983
01:16:27,000 --> 01:16:28,000
Laia: "Yes! "

984
01:16:28,000 --> 01:16:34,000
Narrator: "Virgil handed it to her, and she quickly put it away in one of her bags."

985
01:16:34,000 --> 01:16:37,000
Laia: "Heh, another quest successfully completed!"

986
01:16:37,000 --> 01:16:40,000
Laia: "Now, shall we go? I'm really exhausted."

987
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:41,000
Virgil: "Sur-"

988
01:16:41,000 --> 01:16:46,000
Tamara: "Virgil, it is time to use your new powers for the first time."

989
01:16:46,000 --> 01:16:47,000
Virgil: "Ehh? On her?"

990
01:16:47,000 --> 01:16:51,000
Tamara: "Yeah, she's the perfect v-... test subject!"

991
01:16:51,000 --> 01:16:57,000
