Narrator: "Virgil felt like it was beneath him to do such a thing. "

1394
01:44:58,000 --> 01:45:03,000
Narrator: "Of course, in his naivete, he expected to only take epic quests."

1395
01:45:03,000 --> 01:45:08,000
Isabelle: "Damn, the guild has declined a lot these past years, hasn't it?"

1396
01:45:08,000 --> 01:45:12,000
Isabelle: "They don't teach you about daily quests anymore?"

1397
01:45:12,000 --> 01:45:14,000
Virgil: "Daily quests?"

1398
01:45:14,000 --> 01:45:21,000
Isabelle: "Yeah. There are not enough glorious quests for the dozens and dozens of adventurers out there."

1399
01:45:21,000 --> 01:45:25,000
Isabelle: "So, when days are slow, there are daily quests."

1400
01:45:25,000 --> 01:45:28,000
Virgil: "Sounds like a temp job, to be honest."

1401
01:45:28,000 --> 01:45:36,000
Isabelle: "I guess? Anyhow, you get some easy experience and gold, and it is not like you have anything better to do."

1402
01:45:36,000 --> 01:45:39,000
Virgil: "That's fair. Alright, I'll think about it."

1403
01:45:39,000 --> 01:45:42,000
Isabelle: "Heh, now, let's check the storage room!"

1404
01:45:42,000 --> 01:45:43,000
Virgil: "Ah, sure!"

1405
01:45:43,000 --> 01:45:44,000
*Holy, was that a-*

1406
01:45:44,000 --> 01:45:48,000
Narrator: "Yes, Aldit packed, and even more than Virgil."

1407
01:45:48,000 --> 01:45:51,000
*Okay, I need to be careful around that monster.*

1408
01:45:51,000 --> 01:45:52,000
*Or perhaps not...*

1409
01:45:52,000 --> 01:45:53,000
*......*

1410
01:45:53,000 --> 01:45:54,000
*...*

1411
01:45:54,000 --> 01:45:55,000
*......*

1412
01:45:55,000 --> 01:45:56,000
*...*

1413
01:45:56,000 --> 01:46:00,000
Virgil: "*sigh* What a day. That storage room was truly a mess."

1414
01:46:00,000 --> 01:46:04,000
Tamara: "I can tell something happened, Virgil. What was it?"

1415
01:46:04,000 --> 01:46:07,000
Virgil: "There is no deceiving you, uh?"

1416
01:46:07,000 --> 01:46:13,000
Virgil: "Well, I asked Aldit to sponsor me, but even with my magic, I couldn't persuade her."

1417
01:46:13,000 --> 01:46:16,000
Virgil: "I guess she's just too high level for me."

1418
01:46:16,000 --> 01:46:21,000
Tamara: "You just started, and you are already trying to do this sort of thing?"

1419
01:46:21,000 --> 01:46:24,000
Tamara: "You are ambitious; I can respect that. "

1420
01:46:24,000 --> 01:46:31,000
Tamara: "Sadly, at this rate, it will take you several years before you can persuade someone like her."

1421
01:46:31,000 --> 01:46:36,000
Virgil: "Years? Oh, that's not good. I guess I'll have to grind, then."

1422
01:46:36,000 --> 01:46:38,000
Tamara: "That's it, unless..."

1423
01:46:38,000 --> 01:46:39,000
Virgil: "Unless?..."

1424
01:46:39,000 --> 01:46:40,000
Narrator: "Unless?..."

1425
01:46:40,000 --> 01:46:47,000
Tamara: "I'll help you out one more time, and it will be the last; I don't have the power to do more, anyhow."

1426
01:46:47,000 --> 01:46:49,000
Virgil: "Okay! I'm ready!"

1427
01:46:49,000 --> 01:46:51,000
Tamara: "Of course you are!"

1428
01:46:51,000 --> 01:46:58,000
Narrator: "As the hero was blinded with the magic of the Djinn, he could feel how he was changing."

1429
01:46:58,000 --> 01:47:05,000
Narrator: "Something powerful inside of his soul has awakened, and with that, his fate would be altered again."

1430
01:47:05,000 --> 01:47:07,000
Tamara: "So? How do you feel?"

1431
01:47:07,000 --> 01:47:11,000
Virgil: "Incredible! I really can't describe it, but I feel it!"

1432
01:47:11,000 --> 01:47:18,000
Tamara: "Heh, and this is not even half of what you can achieve, but that will actually take some time."

1433
01:47:18,000 --> 01:47:22,000
Virgil: "so, with this, can I just change Aldit's mind?"

1434
01:47:22,000 --> 01:47:28,000
Tamara: "Not quite... You see, you'll never be able to just snap your fingers and change them."

1435
01:47:28,000 --> 01:47:33,000
Tamara: "But what you can do now is to change them slowly and permanently."

1436
01:47:33,000 --> 01:47:37,000
Tamara: "And for that, you need to have 'control' over them."

1437
01:47:37,000 --> 01:47:38,000
Virgil: "Control?"

1438
01:47:38,000 --> 01:47:47,000
Tamara: "Yes! You now have an aura that allows you to create a strong bond with whomever you interact with for an extended period."

1439
01:47:47,000 --> 01:47:54,000
Tamara: "So, if you spend a few hours with someone, you'll slowly increase this influence you have with them."

1440
01:47:54,000 --> 01:48:06,000
Tamara: "Once this bond is strong enough, you'll be able to break through their mental barriers, and then you will be able to use this control of yours to make changes on them."

1441
01:48:06,000 --> 01:48:09,000
Tamara: "Believe me, it's easier than it sounds!"

1442
01:48:09,000 --> 01:48:13,000
Virgil: "I hope so! I'm still not so sure how this works."

1443
01:48:13,000 --> 01:48:20,000
Tamara: "Look, just spend time with that woman, Aldit, and you'll eventually know when you can change her."

1444
01:48:20,000 --> 01:48:33,000
Tamara: "You won't be able to fully rewrite their mind, though, and some changes will require you to become stronger, but nonetheless, this should suffice for whatever adventure you have ahead."

1445
01:48:33,000 --> 01:48:38,000
Virgil: "Very well! I guess I'll be taking those daily quests after all!"

1446
01:48:38,000 --> 01:48:41,000
Tamara: "Sure. I'm sure we'll have fun!"

1447
01:48:41,000 --> 01:48:48,000
Narrator: "The djinn smirked mysteriously, but Virgil could only speculate about the meaning of this."

1448
01:48:48,000 --> 01:48:50,000
Virgil: "Ehh... Sure, thanks!"

1449
01:48:50,000 --> 01:48:52,000
Tamara: "Now it's time to sleep!"

1450
01:48:52,000 --> 01:48:54,000
Virgil: "Wait, not ag-"

1451
01:48:54,000 --> 01:48:55,000
*......*

1452
01:48:55,000 --> 01:48:56,000
*...*

1453
01:48:56,000 --> 01:49:02,000
*Okay, I need to take this daily quest and grow my control to convince her to support us.*

1454
01:49:02,000 --> 01:49:06,000
*Tamara said this should be easy... I hope it's true. *

1455
01:49:06,000 --> 01:49:11,000
Narrator: "As Virgil approached inside, Aldit's hurried to meet him. "

1456
01:49:11,000 --> 01:49:14,000
Isabelle: "Hey! You came! Want a beer?"

1457
01:49:14,000 --> 01:49:18,000
Virgil: "Actually, I thought about your offer; it's still up? "

1458
01:49:18,000 --> 01:49:23,000
Isabelle: "Really? Sure! I can use your help! The place is always busy!"

1459
01:49:23,000 --> 01:49:28,000
Isabelle: "I didn't think you were going to, but I'm glad you reconsidered it!"

1460
01:49:28,000 --> 01:49:31,000
Virgil: "Aw, did I look that disappointed?"

1461
01:49:31,000 --> 01:49:35,000
Isabelle: "Yeah, you are not that good at hiding your feelings!"

1462
01:49:35,000 --> 01:49:38,000
Isabelle: "Anyhow! Let me show you the place then!"

1463
01:49:38,000 --> 01:49:43,000
Narrator: "Aldit took Virgil and gave him instructions about what to do."

1464
01:49:43,000 --> 01:49:49,000
Narrator: "It wasn't too complicated; he was to stay with her and help her serve drinks."

1465
01:49:49,000 --> 01:49:54,000
Narrator: "For the next few hours, the two of them worked together."

1466
01:49:54,000 --> 01:49:59,000
Narrator: "Although subtle, Virgil could feel how his aura was influencing her."

1467
01:49:59,000 --> 01:50:06,000
Narrator: "When done, the bond with her had grown, but it was still too weak for him to do anything to her."

1468
01:50:06,000 --> 01:50:10,000
Narrator: "But he knew it was only a matter of time."

1469
01:50:10,000 --> 01:50:14,000
Isabelle: "Alright, that wasn't too bad wasn't it, Virgil?"

1470
01:50:14,000 --> 01:50:16,000
Virgil: "No, I guess not!"

1471
01:50:16,000 --> 01:50:22,000
Isabelle: "Heh, okay! Here is your pay, and if you want to keep coming, that'd be great!"

1472
01:50:22,000 --> 01:50:25,000
Virgil: "Sure! I think I will do just that!"

1473
01:50:25,000 --> 01:50:29,000
Isabelle: "Then see you around! And say hi to you landlady for me!"

1474
01:50:29,000 --> 01:50:30,000
Virgil: "Of course!"

1475
01:50:30,000 --> 01:50:33,000
Narrator: "Virgil received 10 XP and 15 gold."

1476
01:50:33,000 --> 01:50:35,000
*Control has increased by 30 points.*

1477
01:50:35,000 --> 01:50:36,000
*......*

1478
01:50:36,000 --> 01:50:37,000
*...*

1479
01:50:37,000 --> 01:50:40,000
*I feel that my bond is very strong now, is she-*

1480
01:50:40,000 --> 01:50:43,000
Tamara: "Hey! Are you ready to do this?"

1481
01:50:43,000 --> 01:50:46,000
Virgil: "Eh?! What are you doing here?!"

1482
01:50:46,000 --> 01:50:50,000
Tamara: "Uh? You know I can move around the city, don't you?"

1483
01:50:50,000 --> 01:50:54,000
Virgil: "Ah? I guess, but it still kinda surprised me!"

1484
01:50:54,000 --> 01:51:01,000
Tamara: "Yeah, I can tell. Anyway! I think your friend here is ready for you to break their mental barriers!"

1485
01:51:01,000 --> 01:51:05,000
Virgil: "Yes, I have the feeling that I could do this."

1486
01:51:05,000 --> 01:51:08,000
Tamara: "You have nice instincts then!"

1487
01:51:08,000 --> 01:51:13,000
Tamara: "To do what's next, you just need to talk with her and focus on her mind."

1488
01:51:13,000 --> 01:51:19,000
Tamara: "You'll see a barrier; pierce through it! And once you do, it will shatter."

1489
01:51:19,000 --> 01:51:25,000
Tamara: "Once that's done, you'll be able to make some changes to her personality."

1490
01:51:25,000 --> 01:51:35,000
Tamara: "Now, remember you will not be able to fully change a person, just a few traits, but that should be enough to make them do what you need."

1491
01:51:35,000 --> 01:51:38,000
Virgil: "Alright, let's do this then!"

1492
01:51:38,000 --> 01:51:45,000
Narrator: "Determined to get what he wanted, Virgil approached his landlady's friend when the place was empty."

1493
01:51:45,000 --> 01:51:47,000
Virgil: "Hey, Aldit, can we talk?"

1494
01:51:47,000 --> 01:51:50,000
Isabelle: "Sure! Why the serious face, though?"

1495
01:51:50,000 --> 01:51:51,000
Virgil: "I just..."

1496
01:51:51,000 --> 01:51:53,000
*Pierce... through... it...*

1497
01:51:53,000 --> 01:51:56,000
Isabelle: "Virgil... what's happening..."

1498
01:51:56,000 --> 01:51:57,000
*Almost... there...*

1499
01:51:57,000 --> 01:52:04,000
Narrator: "The mental barrier of the amazon cracked, and with that, she was open to our hero commands."

1500
01:52:04,000 --> 01:52:08,000
Isabelle: "Ahh! I'm... listening to you... Virgil..."

1501
01:52:08,000 --> 01:52:09,000
*Yes! I got it!*

1502
01:52:09,000 --> 01:52:11,000
Tamara: "See? It wasn't that hard!"

1503
01:52:11,000 --> 01:52:13,000
Virgil: "Indeed! Now what?"

1504
01:52:13,000 --> 01:52:20,000
Tamara: "With this done, you'll be able to get inside her head and mess with it. For now, let's peep..."

1505
01:52:20,000 --> 01:52:27,000
*This is the mind control panel. From here, you'll be able to change your target's mind and traits. *

1506
01:52:27,000 --> 01:52:32,000
*There are three categories: Core personality, Patterns, and Triggers.*

1507
01:52:32,000 --> 01:52:35,000
*Everyone has the same 'core personality' traits.*

1508
01:52:35,000 --> 01:52:38,000
*These are Relationship, Inhibition, and Libido.*

1509
01:52:38,000 --> 01:52:47,000
*Relationship affects how they behave towards you; change it from 'acquaintance' to 'friend' so they are more eager to help you!*

1510
01:52:47,000 --> 01:52:58,000
*Inhibition affects how unashamed they can be; Lower inhibition means they are more willing to exhibit themselves in public, and it may change their outfits too.*

1511
01:52:58,000 --> 01:53:08,000
*Libido affects their needs for sexual satisfaction. Increase it to make it easier to have sex with them. Increase it a lot, and they'll become unsatiable!*

1512
01:53:08,000 --> 01:53:20,000
*If you make them nymphos, it's because you are willing to let them go and have sex around. Don't worry, though; they won't develop feelings, they just need to sate their urges!*

1513
01:53:20,000 --> 01:53:24,000
*Patterns are special personality traits that the person has.*

1514
01:53:24,000 --> 01:53:30,000
*These vary from person to person, and how much you can change them depends on them.*

1515
01:53:30,000 --> 01:53:42,000
*They usually are mild things that you can exacerbate, like making an irritable person into a wrathful one, or turn make a casual gambler addicted to the point of losing everything! *

1516
01:53:42,000 --> 01:53:52,000
*Triggers also vary; generally, they don't make any big changes, but instead, it makes it easier for you to put them again under your control.*

1517
01:53:52,000 --> 01:53:58,000
*In a few words, they usually just reduce the control needed to persuade them to do your will.*

1518
01:53:58,000 --> 01:54:01,000
Virgil: "Alright! Should I try it now? "

1519
01:54:01,000 --> 01:54:05,000
Tamara: "Yes! Let's see if you can get what you want!"

1520
01:54:05,000 --> 01:54:11,000
Tamara: "If you already know what you want to change, just focus and command her. "

1521
01:54:11,000 --> 01:54:12,000
Virgil: "Yes!"

1522
01:54:12,000 --> 01:54:15,000
Virgil: "Listen to me, Aldit, listen!"

1523
01:54:15,000 --> 01:54:17,000
Isabelle: "Yes... I'll listen..."

1524
01:54:17,000 --> 01:54:24,000
Virgil: "I am more than my landlady's tenant]; I am closer to you, like a friend that you can trust."

1525
01:54:24,000 --> 01:54:26,000
Isabelle: "A friend... I trust..."

1526
01:54:26,000 --> 01:54:31,000
Virgil: "Yes! And you want to help your friends in need, don't you?"

1527
01:54:31,000 --> 01:54:34,000
Isabelle: "Yes... I should help them..."

1528
01:54:34,000 --> 01:54:40,000
Virgil: "So, when you turn back to normal... Remember to help me, to become my sponsor."

1529
01:54:40,000 --> 01:54:42,000
Isabelle: "Be... your... sponsor..."

1530
01:54:42,000 --> 01:54:44,000
Virgil: "Correct! Now, wake up!"

1531
01:54:44,000 --> 01:54:47,000
Tamara: "Heh, you know how to do this, don't you?"

1532
01:54:47,000 --> 01:54:50,000
Virgil: "I watched a few shows about hypnotism!"

1533
01:54:50,000 --> 01:54:54,000
Narrator: "And played many, many games about it too..."

1534
01:54:54,000 --> 01:54:56,000
*Hey! How do you know that?!*

1535
01:54:56,000 --> 01:54:58,000
Isabelle: "Virgil? Did I dozed off?"

1536
01:54:58,000 --> 01:55:02,000
Virgil: "No, well... a little! I think you are just tired."

1537
01:55:02,000 --> 01:55:04,000
Isabelle: "Ah, yes, that might be..."

1538
01:55:04,000 --> 01:55:07,000
Virgil: "By the way, can we talk about something?"

1539
01:55:07,000 --> 01:55:09,000
Isabelle: "Sure, about what?"

1540
01:55:09,000 --> 01:55:13,000
Virgil: "You remember that we were talking about the sponsorship?"

1541
01:55:13,000 --> 01:55:15,000
Isabelle: "Ahh... I think so."

1542
01:55:15,000 --> 01:55:18,000
Virgil: "Yes, so... are you going to support us?"

1543
01:55:18,000 --> 01:55:19,000
Isabelle: "I don-"

1544
01:55:19,000 --> 01:55:25,000
Narrator: "Her conflicting feelings and memories made her pause for a brief moment."

1545
01:55:25,000 --> 01:55:32,000
Narrator: "She knew she remembered that conversation very clearly, but right now, it was all foggy."

1546
01:55:32,000 --> 01:55:36,000
Narrator: "Then, the pictures in her brain were as clear as day. "

1547
01:55:36,000 --> 01:55:41,000
Isabelle: "Of course! You asked if I was going to support you, and I will!"

1548
01:55:41,000 --> 01:55:46,000
Virgil: "Correct! So, maybe you can write the letter needed for the guild?"

1549
01:55:46,000 --> 01:55:48,000
Isabelle: "Yes, give me a moment!"

1550
01:55:48,000 --> 01:55:54,000
Narrator: "She hurried to get pen and paper, and soon she had written down the precious letter."

1551
01:55:54,000 --> 01:55:56,000
Isabelle: "Here it is!"

1552
01:55:56,000 --> 01:56:00,000
Virgil: "Thank you a lot, Aldit! You won't regret it!"

1553
01:56:00,000 --> 01:56:04,000
Isabelle: "I know! So far, you have proven yourself... right?"

1554
01:56:04,000 --> 01:56:10,000
Narrator: "Although she said that, she couldn't remember a single feat done by Virgil."

1555
01:56:10,000 --> 01:56:14,000
Narrator: "And yet, she knew he was a man worthy of his word."

1556
01:56:14,000 --> 01:56:16,000
Isabelle: "Is there anything else?"

1557
01:56:16,000 --> 01:56:18,000
Virgil: "No, that'd be all!"

1558
01:56:18,000 --> 01:56:21,000
Isabelle: "Okay, then take care Virgil! "

1559
01:56:21,000 --> 01:56:23,000
*Finally, mission accomplished!*

1560
01:56:23,000 --> 01:56:24,000
*......*

1561
01:56:24,000 --> 01:56:25,000
*...*

1562
01:56:25,000 --> 01:56:31,000
Narrator: "As our hero entered the guild, everyone could tell how determined he looked."

1563
01:56:31,000 --> 01:56:39,000
Narrator: "With Aldit as his sponsor, a renowned veteran, convincing Laia and Rowen to join him wasn't a problem. "

1564
01:56:39,000 --> 01:56:43,000
Narrator: "Now, only bureaucracy was standing in his way."

1565
01:56:43,000 --> 01:56:46,000
Ava: "Hello, Virgil. Did something happen?"

1566
01:56:46,000 --> 01:56:50,000
Virgil: "Yeah! A few things, but all of them positive."

1567
01:56:50,000 --> 01:56:55,000
Virgil: "I am here to create my party! I have my team and a sponsor!"

1568
01:56:55,000 --> 01:56:58,000
Ava: "You do? Okay, let me check that..."

1569
01:56:58,000 --> 01:57:04,000
Narrator: "A few moments later, Ava confirmed that, indeed, Virgil fulfilled every requisite."

1570
01:57:04,000 --> 01:57:09,000
Narrator: "But still, there was something that Virgil didn't expect."

1571
01:57:09,000 --> 01:57:10,000
*Uh?*

1572
01:57:10,000 --> 01:57:17,000
Ava: "Okay, everything is in order. But, we here can reserve the right to approve or not these applications. "

1573
01:57:17,000 --> 01:57:24,000
Ava: "You and your group barely have any real experience; it'd be very negligent of us to allow this to happen."

1574
01:57:24,000 --> 01:57:27,000
Virgil: "What?! But come on, the rules say..."

1575
01:57:27,000 --> 01:57:33,000
Ava: "The rules say many things, more than the few ones said during the induction."

1576
01:57:33,000 --> 01:57:37,000
Ava: "I'm sorry, but I can't allow this to happen. Unless.."

1577
01:57:37,000 --> 01:57:38,000
Virgil: "Unless?"

1578
01:57:38,000 --> 01:57:46,000
Ava: "Well, if you truly insist, I can put you to the test. Show to me that you are capable, and I'll reconsider."

1579
01:57:46,000 --> 01:57:55,000
Narrator: "Although the hero didn't know what was ahead, he was confident that he'd be able to do whatever challenge was put against him."

1580
01:57:55,000 --> 01:57:58,000
Virgil: "Sure! I'll do it. Just tell me what to do."

1581
01:57:58,000 --> 01:58:03,000
Ava: "Great! Then you just need a party member who knows more about nature."

1582
01:58:03,000 --> 01:58:05,000
Virgil: "Laia can take care of that."

1583
01:58:05,000 --> 01:58:08,000
Ava: "Yes, she's the right candidate for it!"

1584
01:58:08,000 --> 01:58:17,000
Ava: "Alright, then you will have to go to the nearby forest. Deep inside, there is a creature that you need to capture and bring here. "

1585
01:58:17,000 --> 01:58:24,000
Ava: "The creature is known as an Alxopagus. It is relatively abundant and not a particularly dangerous one."

1586
01:58:24,000 --> 01:58:32,000
Ava: "Be warned, though; it is as clever as it is swift, and you aren't going to be able to just run towards it and grab it."

1587
01:58:32,000 --> 01:58:37,000
Ava: "As a matter of fact, I'll give you this to aid you with your task."

1588
01:58:37,000 --> 01:58:43,000
Narrator: "The guide handed a curious flask with metal bits and chemicals in them to Virgil. "

1589
01:58:43,000 --> 01:58:49,000
Narrator: "After inspecting it for a brief moment, he would think of it as a 'grenade.'"

1590
01:58:49,000 --> 01:58:54,000
Ava: "This device should be easy to operate, just remove this part and throw it."

1591
01:58:54,000 --> 01:58:59,000
Ava: "Careful! once you activate it, it will blow after five seconds."

1592
01:58:59,000 --> 01:59:09,000
Ava: "It contains something that will put the beast into sleep, and it won't be lethal nor dangerous to you or Laia, but still, you only got one shot."

1593
01:59:09,000 --> 01:59:11,000
Virgil: "Okay, I can handle this!"

1594
