Virgil: "Yes; Laia is at the guild, attending someone... Rowen stayed behind."

2483
03:03:01,000 --> 03:03:04,000
Beatrice: "Attending someone? A prisoner?"

2484
03:03:04,000 --> 03:03:07,000
Virgil: "No, more like a victim of them."

2485
03:03:07,000 --> 03:03:10,000
Beatrice: "Okay, tell me what happened."

2486
03:03:10,000 --> 03:03:11,000
Shael: "Yes, so..."

2487
03:03:11,000 --> 03:03:17,000
Narrator: "The hero and the dark elf told the priestess everything they just faced."

2488
03:03:17,000 --> 03:03:24,000
Narrator: "She listened attentively, and although she appeared to be calm, she was obviously worried. "

2489
03:03:24,000 --> 03:03:30,000
Beatrice: "I see... I fear I will have to report this; we might need outside help."

2490
03:03:30,000 --> 03:03:31,000
Virgil: "Help?"

2491
03:03:31,000 --> 03:03:35,000
Beatrice: "Yes, maybe even ask the inquisition to come."

2492
03:03:35,000 --> 03:03:40,000
Shael: "What?! No way, these cultists are very weak! There is no nee-"

2493
03:03:40,000 --> 03:03:45,000
Beatrice: "There are many things you don't know, Shael, nor you Virgil."

2494
03:03:45,000 --> 03:03:54,000
Shael: "There are many rumors, and these cultists may be related to that... I need to consult someone more knowledgeable, though."

2495
03:03:54,000 --> 03:04:00,000
Shael: "Once I do that, I'll tell you about it since I don't want to speculate nor alarm anyone."

2496
03:04:00,000 --> 03:04:03,000
