Tamara: "I usually wouldn't, but this development it's interesting, so I'm willing to make an exception."

2590
03:10:14,000 --> 03:10:16,000
Virgil: "Great, thanks!"

2591
03:10:16,000 --> 03:10:20,000
Virgil: "Okay, first of all... do you feel it? This magic?"

2592
03:10:20,000 --> 03:10:28,000
Virgil: "When that being just awakened, it felt as if I was inside of a river, so strong that it kept pushing me away."

2593
03:10:28,000 --> 03:10:34,000
Virgil: "Now, though... I still feel a current, but it's just like a puddle in comparison."

2594
03:10:34,000 --> 03:10:37,000
Tamara: "Heh. Do you recognize it too, don't you?"

2595
03:10:37,000 --> 03:10:42,000
Virgil: "...Yes, it's the same magic I use, but it feels different."

2596
03:10:42,000 --> 03:10:45,000
Tamara: "Indeed, that's because this magic is pure."

2597
03:10:45,000 --> 03:10:46,000
Virgil: "Pure?"

2598
03:10:46,000 --> 03:10:56,000
Tamara: "You see, you don't create magic out of nowhere, you channelize it from somewhere, but in this process, it gets tainted, diluted, weakened..."

2599
03:10:56,000 --> 03:11:01,000
Tamara: "The stronger you are, the purer it can be, and therefore more powerful."

2600
03:11:01,000 --> 03:11:06,000
Tamara: "Right now... it is as if the whole city was under a spell of yours."

2601
03:11:06,000 --> 03:11:08,000
Virgil: "What are its effects?"

2602
03:11:08,000 --> 03:11:11,000
Tamara: "Come on, Virgil. Focus, feel it..."

2603
03:11:11,000 --> 03:11:12,000
Virgil: "Okay, mmh..."

2604
03:11:12,000 --> 03:11:18,000
Narrator: "Virgil closed his eyes, and felt the waves of magic crossing through his body."

2605
03:11:18,000 --> 03:11:21,000
Narrator: "Then, he finally got an answer."

2606
03:11:21,000 --> 03:11:25,000
Virgil: "Inhibition... this affects people's inhibition."

2607
03:11:25,000 --> 03:11:27,000
Tamara: "Correct! What else?"

2608
03:11:27,000 --> 03:11:36,000
Virgil: "They... think it's fine, or normal, to dress more lewdly. It's not changing their own personalities, just how they perceive others."

2609
03:11:36,000 --> 03:11:40,000
Tamara: "Well done! See, you don't need me, after all!"

2610
03:11:40,000 --> 03:11:43,000
Virgil: "But I still have other questions."

2611
03:11:43,000 --> 03:11:45,000
Tamara: "Heh, alright, ask then."

2612
03:11:45,000 --> 03:11:47,000
Virgil: "This thing... what is it?"

2613
03:11:47,000 --> 03:11:52,000
Tamara: "I don't know that answer, but I know it is divine in nature."

2614
03:11:52,000 --> 03:11:55,000
Virgil: "Divine? What does that mean?"

2615
03:11:55,000 --> 03:11:59,000
Tamara: "Mmh... to keep it simple, there is a hierarchy."

2616
03:11:59,000 --> 03:12:06,000
Tamara: "At the bottom are mortals, people who can't use nor understand magic. At the top, Gods and Goddesses."

2617
03:12:06,000 --> 03:12:12,000
Tamara: "You are a few steps above a mortal, while I am a few steps under Godhood."

2618
03:12:12,000 --> 03:12:20,000
Tamara: "As a matter of fact, if I hadn't been weakened so much, I'd probably be on my way to becoming a Goddess."

2619
03:12:20,000 --> 03:12:25,000
Tamara: "Heh, can you imagine that? The Goddess of pranks? It'd be so-"

2620
03:12:25,000 --> 03:12:26,000
Virgil: "Ehem..."

2621
03:12:26,000 --> 03:12:28,000
Tamara: "Right, sorry!"

2622
03:12:28,000 --> 03:12:36,000
Tamara: "This being... its energy feels divine, that's as pure as it can get as if it's coming from one of the Gods. "

2623
03:12:36,000 --> 03:12:40,000
Tamara: "But... I don't think it is, at least not exactly one."

2624
03:12:40,000 --> 03:12:47,000
Tamara: "I'd have to investigate more to know its true nature, but I won't get close to it. It is not worth it."

2625
03:12:47,000 --> 03:12:56,000
Tamara: "It might be an emissary or a fragment of one of the Gods. Perhaps once you can communicate with it, you'll be able to find out. "

2626
03:12:56,000 --> 03:12:58,000
Virgil: "It is dangerous?"

2627
03:12:58,000 --> 03:13:02,000
Tamara: "You bet it is! But there is only one way to know. "

2628
03:13:02,000 --> 03:13:05,000
Tamara: "Anything else you want to know?"

2629
03:13:05,000 --> 03:13:10,000
Virgil: "And this wave of magic coming from it... can you tell me more about it?"

2630
03:13:10,000 --> 03:13:19,000
Tamara: "Mmh... This magic is like its body heat; it emanates from her passively, and the stronger it gets, the more powerful it'll become."

2631
03:13:19,000 --> 03:13:30,000
Tamara: "When it got awakened, it did it with a bang, which is why the whole city was drowning on it, but I don't think an event like that will happen again."

2632
03:13:30,000 --> 03:13:38,000
Tamara: "For now, it will affect everyone passively... As it keeps restoring its power, its influence will increase."

2633
03:13:38,000 --> 03:13:41,000
Tamara: "Who knows what other things it can do?"

2634
03:13:41,000 --> 03:13:49,000
Tamara: "Anyway, since the magic is the same as yours, this will likely allow you to do more things with your powers."

2635
03:13:49,000 --> 03:13:50,000
Virgil: "Yeah?"

2636
03:13:50,000 --> 03:13:56,000
Tamara: "Hmm! It is up to you if you want to keep strengthening in the future or not."

2637
03:13:56,000 --> 03:14:01,000
Virgil: "Alright, I'll have to find out more about it before doing that."

2638
03:14:01,000 --> 03:14:03,000
Tamara: "That's a good idea."

2639
03:14:03,000 --> 03:14:05,000
Tamara: "Anything else?"

2640
03:14:05,000 --> 03:14:12,000
Virgil: "Thank you for your help, Tamara. At the very least, it gives me an idea of what I am facing."

2641
03:14:12,000 --> 03:14:14,000
